{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/580091-demon-the-fallen-thread-for-is-better-to-rule-in-earth-than-serve-in-heaven","id":580091,"title":"Demon The Fallen Thread. For is better to Rule in Earth than Serve in Heaven","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-07-05T13:09:05-07:00","id":580091,"title":"Demon The Fallen Thread. For is better to Rule in Earth than Serve in Heaven","content":"Good Evening.<br /> I Am Crowley, i been running DtF for a couple of years now and i noticed that lately, theres been A LOT of questions about one of my favorite games (Demon: The Fallen). For which i decided to make this thread to share ideas, questions, and suggestions about this beautiful game.<br /> I must state a few things before, i have Never read any fiction of DtF (Even if i have Lucifer's Shadow but i havent made the time to read it), and i have never read or lied my eyes upon Houses of The Fallen (Probably because i cant seem able to find it in physical form).<br /> <br /> Other than that, Feel free to ask and suggest what ever you wish and desire.<br /> <br /> Personally, i did a little Homebrewing on the Lores, making them less like &quot;Disciplines&quot; like the ones of Vampires and more in atunnement with the Spheres from Mage. Concidering that demons are Reality Builders in the original sense.<br /> Im not a huge expert on rituals but i can do some little bit more of reseach when it comes to it.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><u>Some of my personal views </u><br /> <br /> To me, Demon the Fallen is a Religious game with a lot of Lovecraftian Overtones. Fill with Regret, Damnation, Depression (Yes. to some degree i found this game AS depressing as Wraith) </span><br /> <br /> <b>The Abyssm</b>: its a Lovecraftian dream come truth, a place fill with hatred, regret and guilt. Always alone but fill with screams of agony (both inside your head and the ones of your Brothers). a Place where you are Always alone (but encapsulated in a way that you can hear others around you). Always dark, Always Hungry (to the point where youre forced to Mutilate yourself and eat your own flesh to survive). A place where the human mind Cant withstand it or Cant Comprehend it.<br /> In my games if ANY creature thats not a demon, gets casted away into the Abysm. He will try to commit suicide just for the sheer horror and theres no way to come back &quot;Sane&quot; from that place, even if youre for less than a minute, your character will be broken in such a way that all his willpower will be erased, his virtues will stop working and you will be a broken shadow of your formerself, only wanting to Die..or perhaps even too afraid of Dying and Going to That place (Had players who thought that bad people went into the Abysm)<br /> <br /> <b>Torment:</b> Its not parasitic, but would almost seem like it. Can you get ridden of it?<br /> In my games, No through outside influence...but Yes through your own Sheer willpower and doing &quot;Good&quot; (that, and 10 exp once your temporal Torment reaches Zero).<br /> <br /> <b>What happends if a Mage &quot;Removes&quot; the torment away?.</b><br /> A sheer experience of the bigest horrors that a Human Mind can see. Even if this were to be ripped out, the pure horror of this eldtrich contamination (IF you wish to see it like this) would go back onto his original Host...but would make the people around do rolls of willpower dificulty 8 and at least 6 successed in order not to go insane for its mere presence.<br /> <br /> <b><u>Character Creation, Whats so Different in your Campaings</u></b><br /> <br /> This is actually interesting. The way I do it its this, i allow the player to Pick a house, Pick his lores (if they are older than the Halaku/Slayers. i give them Lore of Fundament and Humanity) And i allow them to pick their Apocalyptic Forms, Score faith and Score torment..And the Angelic/Demonic Backgrounds (But i dont allow them to start with Thralls or Cult).<br /> Then, i describe how they Break free into The World (and describe towers, buildings, cars and such in the most Eldtrich fashion possible to the Fallen ones).<br /> <br /> Now its where it gets interesting... I dont let them Create the human that they will possess..<br /> I Rather offer them a Number of Humans (with their points already distributed, merits and flaws and such) already done. and once these humans die, i allow the players to get a hold of one of these (the deaths are instant but i give limited time to the player to pick which human to possess).<br /> <br /> I been thinking it a couple of times on doing the process backwards. To allow them to play as a Human and let them Die (for them, it was an accident or a dream) and get the players possessed by demons i Designed with out them notice<br /> <br /> <u><b>What happends when a Demon Dies?</b></u><br /> If you mean erase it out of existance?. on my games at least, i feel that they are a nesesary hook to their creations. What i mean by this?, you cant kill the Angel of Blood (given an example) in a way that you utterly destroy it (NO, I DONT MEAN CONSUME IT. BUT I MEAN AS A MAGE ERASING THIS BEEING OUT OF EXISTANCE) OR his creation will fade with him.<br /> <br /> <i>But what happend with demons which creations dont exist anymore like Unicorns or some rare animals? </i><br /> The creation might be lost, but that doesnt mean that they are out of the game. in a more poetical sense they are &quot;Kings with out a Kingdom to Rule.&quot;<br /> <br /> <i>Ok, But What would change RP wise if my demon created some particular metal?</i><br /> In my games, i allow demons to manipulate more Easly elements that they Created. Yes, this can be overpower if the player knows what he is doing. but the idea is not to let him know until advanced into the game<br /> Example: My trademark character Crowley (Alastor, Angel of Vengeance) is fighting someone just &quot;Because&quot;. if Theres no Implicit vengeance, he uses his lores normally or rolls normal damage.<br /> IF crowley is claiming vengeance upon someone who he belives, deserves to be avenged or punished in the name of Vengeance. Then he has an +1 Damage and his lores related to Vengeance against one individual are -1 difficulty..As long as that individual is Alive or as long the Vengeance is taking place against this individual. The only limit is that Crowley must decide if based upon the thrall story or in whats going on, if its worth to be Avenged. (so yeah, he cant use this bonus if he is avenging you because someone took your parking place. but because of something bigger and epic in scale...Think V For Vendetta or The Crow)<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> These are some of my personal homebrews.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-05T20:36:55-07:00","id":580500,"title":"","content":"I have a question. In a W:tA game I'm running, where I include all of the WoD, a NPC at the high school were the character attend, attempted suicide. She succeeded and died on the way to the hospital. A low level demon than took up residence in her body. The demon is a Devil of the Luciferan faction. She had Social/Mental/Physical as her attribute priorities. She has 3 dots in Lores ( Radiance, The Flame and The Firmament). She has 4 Faith, 4 Torment and 8 Willpower. Her merits are Enchanting voice, Smooth, Good sense of Character, Great Liar, and Good recognition. Her flaws are Abusive Partner and ADD. She was a loner in school and was abused by her father. Nobody in school really noticed her, even the characters, until she killed her self at school. When she came back, she had started dressing differently and made the two girls who had abused her in school into her thralls.<br /> <br /> What I am wanting to know, for this character and for future reference, is what could this demon offer the girls or others to make packs with them. Also is there any way to gain faith without actually making a pack with someone? Thanks for any help you can give.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Reboot","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3684-david-g","name":"David G","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3684_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"176"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-05T20:59:46-07:00","id":580509,"title":"","content":"I never found Demon Lovecraftian myself. To me Lovecraftian would be something extra-universal or some forgotten thing out of spacetime, at least the Demons themselves. Their fortresses and the Earthbound however does have the feel. Lovecraft provoked the fear of the unknown and powerlessness. To me The Wyrm and it's minions are more Lovecraftian designwise. Since Demons are part of the universe and are the reality makers, normal people have better comprehension of a Demon's Apocalyptic Form than say a Nexus Crawler. Like so.<br /> <br /> Demon in Apocalyptic Form<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://vignette2.wikia.nocookie.net/whitewolf/images/9/9c/Demon_the_Fallen_.jpg/revision/latest?cb=20140805180934\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://vignette2.wikia.nocookie.net/whitewolf/images/9/9c/Demon_the_Fallen_.jpg/revision/latest?cb=20140805180934\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://vignette2.wikia.nocookie.net/whitewolf/images/9/9c/Demon_the_Fallen_.jpg/revision/latest?cb=20140805180934\" target=\"_blank\"> http://vignette2.wikia.nocookie.net/whitewolf/images/9/9c/Demon_the_Fallen_.jpg/revision/latest?cb=20140805180934 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Nexus Crawler<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://40.media.tumblr.com/75cd250ac6fde927739ec0b4dd967bd7/tumblr_mxrwd81ixD1rsdg3mo2_1280.png\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://40.media.tumblr.com/75cd250ac6fde927739ec0b4dd967bd7/tumblr_mxrwd81ixD1rsdg3mo2_1280.png\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://40.media.tumblr.com/75cd250ac6fde927739ec0b4dd967bd7/tumblr_mxrwd81ixD1rsdg3mo2_1280.png\" target=\"_blank\"> http://40.media.tumblr.com/75cd250ac6fde927739ec0b4dd967bd7/tumblr_mxrwd81ixD1rsdg3mo2_1280.png </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> It's still a interesting game since you can take your character in three ways; redemption, rule Hell, or be a God. But the only thing I found lacking was antagonists, or lack there of. Yes I know politics is a major factor with WoD which is how Mark Rein-Hagen designed it, but I'm not a political guy. While within the world you got Earthbound, mortals, and other supernaturals, there's one type of antagonist Demon needs but lacks is the Lovecraftian Eldrich Horror. Something not of this universe yet just as powerful or even more than the Demons themselves. Cenobites (yes I give them a honorable mention cause they are not either Angel or Demon but something beyond experience), Elder Things, Old Gods, Caderian spirits ala Evil Dead. I can understand Demons fearing the Earthbound because of the possibility of serving them, but I think having something that even an Earthbound can fear would make a Demon regret going commando.<br /> <br /> Oh, here's a song for you Crowley.<br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=-VT7nJRxJNU\" data-code=\"-VT7nJRxJNU\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/-VT7nJRxJNU/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Onyx Path Kickstarters I back.<br /> W20, MtC, CB20, DtD, MtAs20, BotW20, Wraith 20th.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1442-paladindemo","name":"PaladinDemo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1442_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"622"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-05T21:31:25-07:00","id":580531,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>David G</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/580091-demon-the-fallen-thread-for-is-better-to-rule-in-earth-than-serve-in-heaven?p=580500#post580500\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have a question. In a W:tA game I'm running, where I include all of the WoD, a NPC at the high school were the character attend, attempted suicide. She succeeded and died on the way to the hospital. A low level demon than took up residence in her body. The demon is a Devil of the Luciferan faction. She had Social/Mental/Physical as her attribute priorities. She has 3 dots in Lores ( Radiance, The Flame and The Firmament). She has 4 Faith, 4 Torment and 8 Willpower. Her merits are Enchanting voice, Smooth, Good sense of Character, Great Liar, and Good recognition. Her flaws are Abusive Partner and ADD. She was a loner in school and was abused by her father. Nobody in school really noticed her, even the characters, until she killed her self at school. When she came back, she had started dressing differently and made the two girls who had abused her in school into her thralls.<br /> <br /> What I am wanting to know, for this character and for future reference, is what could this demon offer the girls or others to make packs with them. Also is there any way to gain faith without actually making a pack with someone? Thanks for any help you can give.</div> </div> </div> </div>How to Gain faith with out pacts<br /> If you mean like &quot;Unlock more Faith&quot;? you can go the EXP route<br /> if you mean &quot;Recover more faith&quot;? you can go Four ways.<br /> A ) Reap it (Show one of your miracles or apocalyptic form to a number of humans..this could have Consequences, but you an get a hold of the Faith of the mortals)<br /> B ) Consume IT (Consume another demon esscence, consume its existance before he gets kicked into the abyssm)<br /> C ) Pacts<br /> D ) Sunlight, Every morning as soon as the first light of the sun touches him. he can recover his full Faith<br /> <br /> Gifts for Vapid School girls?..simple, not every gift has to be metaphisical. You can make them popular, you could elaborate some sort of ritual involving your lores and offer them to tell their future and how to avoid problems in the future.<br /> <br /> Remember: Doing pacts with Garous is a bad idea (they will Kill you as soon as you pull it. even if they dont want to kill you)<br /> <br /> <br /> As for Antagonists?<br /> The way i see it, ALL THE WORLD OF DARKNESS WANTS YOU DEAD!<br /> Mages: How many mages would try to get a hold of you and turn you into a Slave? or rather, how many of them would try to kill you because of the perception of every demon beeing &quot;Evil.&quot;<br /> Hunters: ...Goes with out saying<br /> Garous: you are a physical manifestation of Corruption to them...what do you think it will happend?<br /> Wraiths: Those who know the truth will send in for your arse<br /> Spectres: oooohhh boy, the ammount of angst in these guys and the ways they will Try to use you<br /> Vampires: See Mages.<br /> Technocracy: You are an Alien. They are The Space Marines.<br /> Mummies: ....seriously?<br /> The Camarilla: Youre the LIVING PROOF THAT CAIN EXISTED! AND THEY DONT WISH PEOPLE TO BELIVE IN THE EXISTANCE OF HIM OR THE PRIMOGENIANS!<br /> The Sabbath: YOURE THE LIVING PROOF THAT THERE WILL BE A GEHENNA! ONE OF THEIR CLANS IS MODELED AFTER YOU!!<br /> The Wyrm/Pentex: YOURE A ROCKSTAR AMONG EVIL GUYS! YOURE THE CHARLIE MANSON OF CORRUPTION INCORPORATED!!<br /> Faes: youre what nightmares are made Of.<br /> Twilight Project: ...Ever seen Twin Peaks?<br /> Kindread of East:...i Dunno, i never read it. not planning too (way to complex for me)<br /> Nephandi: See wyrm/pentex<br /> Marauders: COLOUR TWELVE!!<br /> <br /> I think i touched upon them all.<br /> To me, Demon is a game about &quot;The price of having the power.&quot; since everyone wants a bite out of you for their own selfish acts<br /> <br /> Speaking of Supernaturals...<br /> <br /> <b>How do garous explain The existance of demons?</b><br /> This hasnt been properly brought up in any book that i remember. I had this discussion with an old friend about their existance and this is What i use in My Games ( i might be wrong on the garou perspective, lemme know if im fudging things or if sounds like a paussable scenario or not)<br /> <br /> To me..Demons are Gaia related Incarnae, probably Majin Incarnae who were to take a role in all of Creation. But once the wyrm went insane, these also started to get corrupted and twisted. So Gaia punished them by casting them away to a prision made of their own madness, almost like the Wyrm.<br /> Letting the Shapeshifters take over the roles of these Incarnae as protectors of her and warriors over the creations of the Incarnae (without them knowing)<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>How do Fae explain the existance of Demons?</b><br /> <br /> I repeat, i dont belive this has been properly brought in any game so im making things up as i go with the little knowledge i got on Changeling, if im wrong or i sound way too far stretch, lemme know..if you got a better explanation let me know.<br /> <br /> To me, in my perception and for what little i know about Changelings.<br /> <br /> I belive that to the Changelings - Demons are actually a collective nightmare that came from the fear of the unknown before everything existed. An idea of repulsive fear and nightmares, pure destructive caos that was sealed in order to protect the dreaming and the dreams of mindkind itself from a figure so Alien and so Mind shattering that, as a collective. could be the primordial Nightmare before the idea of Dreaming even existed.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-05T21:51:00-07:00","id":580537,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crowley</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/580091-demon-the-fallen-thread-for-is-better-to-rule-in-earth-than-serve-in-heaven?p=580531#post580531\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>How do garous explain The existance of demons?</b><br /> This hasnt been properly brought up in any book that i remember. I had this discussion with an old friend about their existance and this is What i use in My Games ( i might be wrong on the garou perspective, lemme know if im fudging things or if sounds like a paussable scenario or not)<br /> <br /> To me..Demons are Gaia related Incarnae, probably Majin Incarnae who were to take a role in all of Creation. But once the wyrm went insane, these also started to get corrupted and twisted. So Gaia punished them by casting them away to a prision made of their own madness, almost like the Wyrm.<br /> Letting the Shapeshifters take over the roles of these Incarnae as protectors of her and warriors over the creations of the Incarnae (without them knowing)</div> </div> </div> </div>Incarnae are beyond stats, and somewhat more focused than elohim on anything, since they're deputies of the Celestines that picked them from the jaggling spirits and represent a part of the Celestine's domain. Also, Maeljin are all corrupt from their very inception rather than pure things gone awry, filth passed down from filth passed down from the entrapment of Balance. Anything from the Triatic Wyrms down in the modern hierarchy of the Wyrm is a thing born of madness and corruption with no prior existence as a great and noble fallen being. You'd have to search for beings outside of Malfeas to find any of those, if they even exist.<br /> <br /> Werewolf was about as antithetical to Demon as it was to Mage, with the added flourish of the Fallen never getting any kind of filtered antagonist shorthand to describe their existence. It was so far away from the concerns of W:tA that what you would get probably wouldn't even kind of resemble D:tF characters even if you tilted your head sideways and squinted. Just consider the difference between the presentation of Bezariel in Rage Across Russia, and his presentation in Earthbound.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-05T22:33:51-07:00","id":580553,"title":"","content":"Thank you very much, Crowley, this helps a lot and has given me ideas. This demon is just to give them a taste of what a demon could be like. I have a long running plot involving a demon worshiping cult that is trying to summon a powerful demon. The demon is Raziel, who in Jewish folklore gave Adam and Eve a book that explained how the universe worked. Since there are numerous legends from around the planet about gods giving man knowledge against the wishes of their kind, I wrapped them up into Raziel. Of course the book has been long lost to the ages. The cult has a fragment of it and are going to try to use it to summon Raziel. They have kidnapped a kid from the high school about a month ago game time. This kid is a local preacher's son who preached in the commons area of the school. Most of the kids heckled him every day. But the kid had True Faith and continued every day. He had done this for years before so no one took him seriously. The characters really haven't been trying to find out what happened, as other things kept sidetracking them. But they have recently gotten some clues. The cult chose the kid because of who he is and are under the impression that if they break him and despoil him he will make a perfect vessel for Raziel. The reason they are going after Raziel is they have learned of him, but not his true name from other demons that they have summoned for knowledge. Their goal is to summon Raziel, make a pact with him for knowledge and power in exchange for an earthly body. The characters have a window of opportunity to save the kid. My goal is to have them interrupt the summon ritual, but in the carnage Raziel is freed accidentally and takes the boy anyway. I am having the boys True Faith protect his soul and finally allow him peaceful transit to his just reward. During the fight, his body will give out and this is time to happen as Raziel is freed from the summoning circle. I'm going to allow the boys utter faith to help Raziel as he inhabits the boys body. Raziel will end up with Faith of 5, Torment of 4 and willpower of 8. He will have 24 dots in lores, but not right away, he will &quot;acquire&quot; them at 3 dots every other day after he assumes the boys body. Raziel has the following backgrounds: Eminence 4, Legacy 5. He has the following merits: Angelic Gaze, Angelic Aura, Dreams from the past, Supportive family, and Approachable. His flaws stem from his human host: Allergies, Honest to a Fault, Youthful appearance, and Stalked. When he gets his full lores, he will have: Awakening 4, The Fundament 5, Humanity 2, Light 2, Patterns 3, Portals 4, Radiance 2, Realms 2. His nature is Perfectionist, with Visionary as his demeanor. He is a Fiend, visage of Portals, of the reconciler faction.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Reboot","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3684-david-g","name":"David G","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3684_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"176"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-05T23:18:26-07:00","id":580572,"title":"","content":"These are absolutely inspired Crowley. Thank you for collecting these rules into one spot. Ever think about doing your own website where you can store your rules in one spot for everyone to see? <br /> <br /> Also, what are your thoughts on the remainder of demons still in Hell? Not the higher ups, like Fell Knights, but the ordinary that might not have left. There are rules for summoning demons from The Pit, and I am thinking about pitching a game where the characters can summon, and possibly bind, their own Infernal Court.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-05T23:56:52-07:00","id":580589,"title":"","content":"Typinvg from The cellphone.<br /> <br /> One: according to Days of Fire , there 99.999.999.999.999 elohim, but it also states that theres &quot;One place for an elohim. An elohim for a place&quot;. And that one quarter fell into The Abysm. And 666 are Earthbounds<br /> <br /> Now, as for Raziel...lemme give ya a little piece of advice from someone who learn The rough way... Bear in mind, my demon was Tony Crowley. <br /> He was The Son of Aliester Crowley who was sacrificed in order to summon Death -very a la Sandman- and got Alastor instead. ( one Day i can tell ya his story) <br /> Now, being Alastor in The Human World was a pain. Why? Because EVERY TIME A MORTAL SAID HIS NAME, HE WAS AWARE OF IT. SO IMAGINE LIVING WITH CONSTANT WHATSSAP MESSAGES RINGING ON, 24/7, NO MUTE BUTTON AND NO WAY TO PULL IT OFF OR STOP IT.<br /> <br /> So, as a personal advice. Raz gotta be a little more insane than usual..think like The M\u00e1ster from doctor who. Alwats seeing The faces of whomever says yer NAME. Thats one little price of having a popular NAME <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> that and being easy to get to.<br /> My char's been around since 1915 (thank you Aliester) and he learned to ignore it after almost 60 years. And with Raz being that popular IMAGINE The sheer ammount of pressure a Human would get from seeing faces and listening to random people using THAT NAME everyday, specially on an era where Soul Reaver is a Thing<br /> <br /> <br /> As for The Website thing? Im too lazy for it, if someone does it for me. Ill be down with it<br /> <br /> Kudos to Draconomicon from The WoD forums who thought me The basis on DtF.<br /> <br /> Oh ad David, careful with True Faith. Its este to find, as rare to find as a Virgin over 23.<br /> Having True Faith and having a demon involved is as dangerous as having a moth covered in fuel heading to a bug zapper.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":1754,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","user":"Crowley","date":". 07-06-2015, 03:10 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-06T01:17:48-07:00","id":580626,"title":"","content":"I think the changelings might see demons as the nightmares of uncreation who became trapped (and thus tormented) within their own nightmare.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-06T01:43:04-07:00","id":580661,"title":"","content":"Or, perhaps more poetically, the Fallen might be seen as the nightmares of eternal darkness by the Light-bringer, Lugh (similar to Loki, whose name means something like 'light-bringer'). Thus the Abyss is his nightmare of eternal darkness, where his children/siblings/heroes are kept (Lugh sired monsters and heroes like Loki, I believe).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-06T07:47:28-07:00","id":580944,"title":"","content":"The World is after you is a given. But considering that Demons has complete control over the universe, the only ones I can see as a real threat would be Archmages and Mummies. Both have the capability of matching Demons' Lore abilities.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Onyx Path Kickstarters I back.<br /> W20, MtC, CB20, DtD, MtAs20, BotW20, Wraith 20th.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1442-paladindemo","name":"PaladinDemo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1442_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"622"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-06T08:08:24-07:00","id":580961,"title":"","content":"Hey, thanks for the input Crowley, but let me clarify that only the boy had True Faith, Raziel only has the boy's memories of having such strong faith. Also Raziel is may not be his true name as he is also known as Raziel, Razeel, Razial, Ratziel, and Galizur. And with my thinking that he is also the same being from other legends about divine beings giving knowledge to man, he is known by many other names such a Prometheus, Quetzalcoatl, etc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Reboot","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3684-david-g","name":"David G","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3684_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"176"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-06T13:38:50-07:00","id":581459,"title":"","content":"Hey, anybody notice this yet?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://m.youtube.com/watch?v=X4bF_quwNtw\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://m.youtube.com/watch?v=X4bF_quwNtw\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://m.youtube.com/watch?v=X4bF_quwNtw\" target=\"_blank\"> https://m.youtube.com/watch?v=X4bF_quwNtw </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-06T16:30:09-07:00","id":581689,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mercurial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/580091-demon-the-fallen-thread-for-is-better-to-rule-in-earth-than-serve-in-heaven?p=581459#post581459\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hey, anybody notice this yet?<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://m.youtube.com/watch?v=X4bF_quwNtw\" target=\"_blank\">https://m.youtube.com/watch?v=X4bF_quwNtw</a></div> </div> </div> </div>...It has NOTHING TO DO WITH THE BEAUTIFUL DC VERTIGO COMIC!!...its more, it reminds me of my character (Crowley) xD","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-07T10:24:39-07:00","id":582478,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the answers to my questions Crowley. What you said about Raziel being a well known name got me to thinking. Should I give him a +2 difficulty to all of his rolls to do anything to represent the distractions?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Reboot","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3684-david-g","name":"David G","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3684_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"176"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-07T11:14:27-07:00","id":582530,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>David G</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/580091-demon-the-fallen-thread-for-is-better-to-rule-in-earth-than-serve-in-heaven?p=582478#post582478\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks for the answers to my questions Crowley. What you said about Raziel being a well known name got me to thinking. Should I give him a +2 difficulty to all of his rolls to do anything to represent the distractions?</div> </div> </div> </div>personally, i would. at least for a while since he is always listening to people calling his name.<br /> Crowley learned to block that shit after a couple o' years, a sort of &quot;Selective hearing.&quot;<br /> <br /> Now, Raz would have some difficulty when it comes to social stuff or when it needs concentration...and im pretty sure he woudnt talk but rather Shout for a while, same with perception rolls","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-08T11:44:15-07:00","id":583686,"title":"","content":"Here is another question. When does a demon's apocalyptic form manifest? How would other supernaturals notice a demon or see its apocalyptic form? Would the merit true sight see a demon for what it really is? (Sorry, a lot more questions)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Reboot","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3684-david-g","name":"David G","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3684_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"176"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-08T20:46:19-07:00","id":584116,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>David G</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/580091-demon-the-fallen-thread-for-is-better-to-rule-in-earth-than-serve-in-heaven?p=583686#post583686\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here is another question. When does a demon's apocalyptic form manifest? How would other supernaturals notice a demon or see its apocalyptic form? Would the merit true sight see a demon for what it really is? (Sorry, a lot more questions)</div> </div> </div> </div>in order<br /> One: Whenever the demon wants<br /> Two: Depends, Does the supernatural knows the Fallen Host from before?<br /> If so, there might be changes in the personality, habits and some other things that might seem 'Off' at first if the demon doesnt follows his &quot;Human&quot; nature.<br /> If not, perhaps something off, the scent, the lifeless eyes in a way, some small details (perception + awarness difficulty 10 if the demon has very low Torment, after torment 5, you start getting lower difficulties to notice it. if the demon has torment 6 , then the difficulty is 9. if the demon has torment 7, the diff is 8 and so on.)<br /> <br /> True Sight...ok this is complex. The way I interpret this is like the Hunter's Second Sight. it DOEST GIVES AWAY..but it gives little glimpses and little tells, very subtil things..Think &quot;Sherlock Vision.&quot;<br /> <br /> Example:<br /> Adam Wong is a human with True Sight, he has seen things for a long long time but never interacted with them. He is getting a musical deal and now he must meet his producer. He arrives to a recording studio where he is having an interview with Thomas Antony Crowley. he rolls perception to notices a couple of off things (3 successes and one critical hit with a 10).<br /> Crowley ALWAYS wear his rayban sunglasses, even when its dark..he rolls int and he fails. - Perhaps Crowley has some sort of problem with Lights.<br /> He keeps examinating this man as he notices that the Shadows around him sort of caste a weird figure around him, he rolls int and he gets one success..he notices that theres some equipment lying around that produce a &quot;Wings&quot; effect over his shadow<br /> he rolls perception again and notices other Off thing, Crowley never blinks...Weird, perhaps related to his eye condition?.<br /> one last perception roll and also notices him being almost Ivory White and that his Shadow has weird elements on it, Not just the wings but little flickers..also that he Doesnt Sweat in general...and the weird fact that sometimes he talks usually but upon touching the religious subject or the &quot;Human Will&quot; subject, his persona shifts from the &quot;Cellphone Fast Talker, Tongue and cheek ironic son of a bitch and almost scottish bastard.&quot; to something more...Dettached, Omnious and he looses his accent, he seems to be almost in a Cloud from which he sees the speakers down as if they were kids or childs, as some sort of Elevated person...<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-08T21:48:52-07:00","id":584169,"title":"","content":"Thanks Crowley, That helps a lot. In the game I am running (W:tA) the characters have interacted with a Fallen who has taken over a girl who tried to kill herself. The have noticed something isn't right with her. She was a nobody in school and since she has been back she has a small following of girls that hang on her every word. They grew suspicious and used various gifts to try to figure out what she is. In my game I run the Fallen as showing up as all three types of beings, ie Wyrn, Wyld and Weaver. They have used all three sense gifts on her. They are confused now since sense Wyrm failed (character botched her roll) they don't know what to think. Also they did this at school and the Fallen felt them using their gifts and zeroed in on them and looked directly at them when ever they did this. Which creeped them out even more. The characters have a kinfolk with true sight, but he hasn't been around. They talked to one of their elders, and he asked if they had sensed Wyrm on her. Since they failed the roll, they told him no. He told them to be careful, keep an eye on her, but unless she did something, that it wasn't their concern. All the Fallen is doing so far has been getting some thralls and giving them what they want.(Popularity and the envy of other students). But the characters keep snooping on the Fallen and she is getting frustrated. She can sense that they are using some sort of magic, but she doesn't know what and doesn't yet know that the characters a Garou. Which by the way, she knows nothing about. So that is a question I need to ask, would a Fallen feel anything when seeing a Garou in Crinos form? Basically, would the racial memory of the Garou come through in the thoughts and feelings Basically from her host? Or since her host never has had any experience with Garou, would the Fallen just react normally. Basically, seeing a monster in front of her and act accordingly. <br /> <br /> If the characters are smart, they could learn a lot from this Fallen. First, she's new and not very powerful. but she does have some knowledge, especially about Raziel. Raziel hasn't arrived yet, but will shortly. Game time about 2 weeks. This is why I have been asking all these questions. I really appreciate all of your answers. I've read the books, but there is just so much, and that's not the game I am currently running. I like Demon, and would enjoy playing it. (about the only game I didn't like was Wraith).<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Reboot","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3684-david-g","name":"David G","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3684_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"176"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-08T23:29:59-07:00","id":584293,"title":"","content":"She won't be subjected to the Veil if that makes is what you are asking. Demons are very specifically immune to mental manipulation powers. So, yeah. The demon will just see a movie monster and react accordingly. <br /> <br /> The Garou, however, will almost certainly figure she is some sort of Fomori.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-09T19:20:16-07:00","id":585526,"title":"","content":"I have another question, what happens when a Fallen is summoned while in a host body?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Reboot","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3684-david-g","name":"David G","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3684_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"176"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-09T20:53:27-07:00","id":585591,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>David G</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/580091-demon-the-fallen-thread-for-is-better-to-rule-in-earth-than-serve-in-heaven?p=585526#post585526\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have another question, what happens when a Fallen is summoned while in a host body?</div> </div> </div> </div>in my terms? the body of the human falls into a sort of coma as the demon appears infront of the humans, he cant be bound since he is already linked to another body.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-09T21:40:23-07:00","id":585642,"title":"","content":"Thanks, that helps out a lot. Especially if Raziel gets to settle into his new life.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Reboot","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3684-david-g","name":"David G","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3684_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"176"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-11T00:53:20-07:00","id":586910,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PaladinDemo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/580091-demon-the-fallen-thread-for-is-better-to-rule-in-earth-than-serve-in-heaven?p=580509#post580509\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I never found Demon Lovecraftian myself. To me Lovecraftian would be something extra-universal or some forgotten thing out of spacetime, at least the Demons themselves. Their fortresses and the Earthbound however does have the feel. Lovecraft provoked the fear of the unknown and powerlessness. To me The Wyrm and it's minions are more Lovecraftian designwise. Since Demons are part of the universe and are the reality makers, normal people have better comprehension of a Demon's Apocalyptic Form than say a Nexus Crawler.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ohhhh.... there's Lovecraftian elements. Lemme tell you about the Earthbound.... They've gone totally batshit crazy. Not like a little bit crazy, like so crazy that even other insane Fallen look at them funny.<br /> In the Earthbound book, they have Lore that allows them to pull unnatural things from beyond the universe and force them into the World of Darkness to do their bidding. Creatures from the elemental chaos of nothing that existed before creation. And Earthbound are willing to use those things. AND LET THEM IN.<br /> <br /> ^_^<br /> <br /> Does that conform more with what you wanted? I mean, you mentioned the Earthbound but you didn't mention the things they consort with....<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crowley</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/580091-demon-the-fallen-thread-for-is-better-to-rule-in-earth-than-serve-in-heaven?p=580531#post580531\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>How do garous explain The existance of demons?</b><br /> This hasnt been properly brought up in any book that i remember. I had this discussion with an old friend about their existance and this is What i use in My Games ( i might be wrong on the garou perspective, lemme know if im fudging things or if sounds like a paussable scenario or not)</div> </div> </div> </div>My friend and I were debating this, because I can't stand the Garou pantheon/whatever (wyrm/wyld/weaver). He thinks they just totally misremember the Angels and have telephone gamed the real events.<br /> <br /> I think all those weaver or wyld or wyrm spirits are actually the industrial equipment Angels/Demons used to build the world, left abandonned and... oh hey started working all on their own. Oops.<br /> <br /> Hell, the Reapers BUILT the umbra!<br /> <br /> Crowley, I want to thank you for starting this thread. I found it by accident, but I've loved it. I ADORE DEMON! I was a big fan of the Hunter setting, and read those and other similar books (Demon Hunter X, Hunter's Hunted, Halls of the Arcanum, Project Twilight, The Inquisition) ravenously, but when I found Demon I was like &quot;This. This is the best thing White Wolf has ever done.&quot; Sadly no one agrees with me, and I've never once gotten to use my Demon books for more than light reading. But GAH! The potential. I love this setting.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6883-darkexcalibur42","name":"DarkExcalibur42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6883_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-11T00:56:20-07:00","id":586911,"title":"","content":"Oh, right. The original reason I went Google searching and found this thread was that I heard a rumor that there were actual rules printed for reaching zero torment and reclaiming your angelic status (which I assumed had some rules and/or statistical reward associated), but have found nothing so far. Does such a thing exist?<br /> <br /> OH! Page 90, Time of Judgement. Nevermind! I'll just be here enjoying the conversation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":6883,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6883-darkexcalibur42","user":"DarkExcalibur42","date":". 07-11-2015, 04:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6883-darkexcalibur42","name":"DarkExcalibur42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6883_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-11T07:21:19-07:00","id":587074,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkExcalibur42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/580091-demon-the-fallen-thread-for-is-better-to-rule-in-earth-than-serve-in-heaven?p=586910#post586910\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> My friend and I were debating this, because I can't stand the Garou pantheon/whatever (wyrm/wyld/weaver). He thinks they just totally misremember the Angels and have telephone gamed the real events.<br /> <br /> I think all those weaver or wyld or wyrm spirits are actually the industrial equipment Angels/Demons used to build the world, left abandonned and... oh hey started working all on their own. Oops.<br /> <br /> Hell, the Reapers BUILT the umbra!</div> </div> </div> </div>Crowley asked how Werewolf would explain Demon, not how Demon would explain Werewolf.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-11T10:03:40-07:00","id":587226,"title":"","content":"Look at his post when I mentioned the lack of antagonists.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Onyx Path Kickstarters I back.<br /> W20, MtC, CB20, DtD, MtAs20, BotW20, Wraith 20th.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1442-paladindemo","name":"PaladinDemo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1442_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"622"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-11T11:02:27-07:00","id":587248,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/580091-demon-the-fallen-thread-for-is-better-to-rule-in-earth-than-serve-in-heaven?p=587074#post587074\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Crowley asked how Werewolf would explain Demon, not how Demon would explain Werewolf.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep. That's how they would explain it: wrong. ^_^<br /> <br /> They'd probably assume all demons were insane or corrupted wyrm spirits or banes. They look wyrm tainted most of the time when werewolves look at them, so why would you trust anything they said? They're obviously powerful spirits, too. So it makes sense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6883-darkexcalibur42","name":"DarkExcalibur42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6883_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-12T10:48:40-07:00","id":588313,"title":"","content":"So what happens if a Vampire drinks from a Demon?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my DriveThruRPG books at: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?author=Carrie%20Kube\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse....=Carrie%20Kube</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1834-yaoi-huntress-earth","name":"Yaoi Huntress Earth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1834_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"535"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-12T11:56:11-07:00","id":588348,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yaoi Huntress Earth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/580091-demon-the-fallen-thread-for-is-better-to-rule-in-earth-than-serve-in-heaven?p=588313#post588313\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So what happens if a Vampire drinks from a Demon?</div> </div> </div> </div>nothing, the human host feels pleasure.<br /> <br /> in my game, depends on how much torment does the demon holds, the blood might be painful to drink. might even drive the vampire to have nightmares or visions.<br /> <br /> <br /> As for villians, if i dont bad remember, someone in the forums was working in Nephilim (I think it was you Yaoi Huntress Earth). but if im wrong i apologize.<br /> <br /> on my game i had the idea of a group of Angels that managed to &quot;Escape&quot; and &quot;Forget&quot; in a way. full angels who use and manipulate humanity into doing their bidding so they can &quot;Reach God&quot; by destroying the world for Her. very influenced by characters like Kaoru Nagisa.<br /> <br /> The other villians i had was the Dark Crussade, but rather than a villian was an organization of Wyrm Followers leaded by an Earthbound who wanted to destroy everything and leave the earth for the Childes of The Wyrm<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-12T13:13:38-07:00","id":588416,"title":"","content":"Thanks for all the info Crowley, but I have another question. How many pacts can a Demon have at one time. Pacts are listed as backgrounds, and they usually only go to five. But in most of the games that I have played we have ruled that that was for starting characters. Since people like Bill Gates have resources way above 5 and they are normal humans. So would you allow pacts above five or is there some reason not to.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Reboot","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3684-david-g","name":"David G","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3684_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"176"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-12T15:38:59-07:00","id":588518,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crowley</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/580091-demon-the-fallen-thread-for-is-better-to-rule-in-earth-than-serve-in-heaven?p=588348#post588348\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> nothing, the human host feels pleasure.<br /> <br /> in my game, depends on how much torment does the demon holds, the blood might be painful to drink. might even drive the vampire to have nightmares or visions.<br /> <br /> <br /> As for villians, if i dont bad remember, someone in the forums was working in Nephilim (I think it was you Yaoi Huntress Earth). but if im wrong i apologize.<br /> <br /> on my game i had the idea of a group of Angels that managed to &quot;Escape&quot; and &quot;Forget&quot; in a way. full angels who use and manipulate humanity into doing their bidding so they can &quot;Reach God&quot; by destroying the world for Her. very influenced by characters like Kaoru Nagisa.<br /> <br /> The other villians i had was the Dark Crussade, but rather than a villian was an organization of Wyrm Followers leaded by an Earthbound who wanted to destroy everything and leave the earth for the Childes of The Wyrm<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know, I might fluff something up depending on the type of demon it is, drinking a devourer might make you more prone to frenzy while drinking a devil may give you an automatic success on charisma or manipulation rolls. I would definately add either angelic visions or demonic nightmares depending on the torment rating at time of blood sucking though","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/359-dezeroth","name":"Dezeroth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar359_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"496"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-12T21:16:06-07:00","id":588837,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>David G</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/580091-demon-the-fallen-thread-for-is-better-to-rule-in-earth-than-serve-in-heaven?p=588416#post588416\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks for all the info Crowley, but I have another question. How many pacts can a Demon have at one time. Pacts are listed as backgrounds, and they usually only go to five. But in most of the games that I have played we have ruled that that was for starting characters. Since people like Bill Gates have resources way above 5 and they are normal humans. So would you allow pacts above five or is there some reason not to.</div> </div> </div> </div>There isn't really any suggestion that there is a limit to how many pacts you can earn. Just have a good social stat and be mindful of what people need. Lots of people wasting away that would do anything to be well. Lots of widows with children would do anything for good health, money, a new mate. And if all else fails you can always offer up the numbers to next weeks winning Lotto if you have Lore of Patterns.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","user":"Mercurial","date":". 07-13-2015, 12:19 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-12T21:38:20-07:00","id":588852,"title":"","content":"Thanks Mercurial, the demon in question has a charisma and manipulation of 4 each. She only has 3 pots in Lores but is very good at getting what she wants socially. She's starting with girls at school and then using them to get to their parents.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Reboot","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3684-david-g","name":"David G","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3684_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"176"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-13T09:14:55-07:00","id":589288,"title":"","content":"If this is serving as our makeshift &quot;general Demon thread&quot;, I'd like to get folks' input on a project I've been toying with for a while.<br /> <br /> I've been trying to come up with a few new or &quot;alternate&quot; Evocations for each of the House Lores. This has proven difficult, though, whether because I am not sure how to expand a given Lore's themes, or because my idea for a new Evocation turns out to be very similar to a Ritual from the Player's Guide.<br /> <br /> So, I present three sample ideas for new Evocations, and I ask your help in refining and statting them:<br /> <br /> <b>Winds 1 or 2: Listen to the Wind</b><br /> Low Torment: Conveys sound towards or awayfrom someone (useful for stealth, communication, reconnaisance)<br /> High Torment: Deadens all sound in a zone around the Demon (and perhaps causes paranoia in nearby mortals?)<br /> <br /> <b>Portals 3: Call to Hand</b><br /> Low Torment: pull one of the demon's possessions to them across a great distance<br /> High Torment: damages the item in-transit<br /> <br /> <b>Death 3 or 4: Suspend Death</b><br /> Low Torment: keep dying person from immediately passing on (such as to buy time for an ambulance to arrive)<br /> High Torment: inflicts derangement, or perhaps steals life from others in area (including the Demon)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr />Avatar commissioned from the incomparable Melissa Uran.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/966-redford_blade","name":"Redford_Blade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar966_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"90"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-13T11:28:50-07:00","id":589412,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Redford_Blade</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/580091-demon-the-fallen-thread-for-is-better-to-rule-in-earth-than-serve-in-heaven?p=589288#post589288\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If this is serving as our makeshift &quot;general Demon thread&quot;, I'd like to get folks' input on a project I've been toying with for a while.</div> </div> </div> </div>I kinda hope so? It's the only part of this forum I'm actually following, and I'm quite eager to discuss any element of Demon.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I've been trying to come up with a few new or &quot;alternate&quot; Evocations for each of the House Lores. This has proven difficult, though, whether because I am not sure how to expand a given Lore's themes, or because my idea for a new Evocation turns out to be very similar to a Ritual from the Player's Guide.<br /> <br /> So, I present three sample ideas for new Evocations, and I ask your help in refining and statting them:<br /> <br /> <b>Winds 1 or 2: Listen to the Wind</b><br /> Low Torment: Conveys sound towards or awayfrom someone (useful for stealth, communication, reconnaisance)<br /> High Torment: Deadens all sound in a zone around the Demon (and perhaps causes paranoia in nearby mortals?)<br /> <br /> <b>Portals 3: Call to Hand</b><br /> Low Torment: pull one of the demon's possessions to them across a great distance<br /> High Torment: damages the item in-transit<br /> <br /> <b>Death 3 or 4: Suspend Death</b><br /> Low Torment: keep dying person from immediately passing on (such as to buy time for an ambulance to arrive)<br /> High Torment: inflicts derangement, or perhaps steals life from others in area (including the Demon) </div> </div> </div>I think that the Lore is purposely limited in its scope on purpose, but I'll at least give you some feedback (though I won't call it expert feedback, at least it's another perspective).<br /> <br /> I think the Wind ability sounds really cool actually! The high torment thing seems like something out of a horror movie where the winds are practically whispering around people.<br /> <br /> Portals all directly deal with actual portals (doorways), so for the call to hand power.... wouldn't they need to reach into a bag or something for it to work?<br /> <br /> Suspend Death seems iffy to me. The Lore of Death all deals with causing death.or predicting the end, so it doesn't seem like it fits. It seems like it might fit more with Lore of the Spirit or Awakening.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6883-darkexcalibur42","name":"DarkExcalibur42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6883_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-13T14:16:16-07:00","id":589518,"title":"","content":"Hey, just came by for a moment..Want some interesting inspiration for earthbounds?<br /> Check Mr.B Gone by Clive Barker <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-13T19:09:54-07:00","id":589790,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkExcalibur42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/580091-demon-the-fallen-thread-for-is-better-to-rule-in-earth-than-serve-in-heaven?p=589412#post589412\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that the Lore is purposely limited in its scope on purpose, but I'll at least give you some feedback (though I won't call it expert feedback, at least it's another perspective).<br /> <br /> I think the Wind ability sounds really cool actually! The high torment thing seems like something out of a horror movie where the winds are practically whispering around people.<br /> <br /> Portals all directly deal with actual portals (doorways), so for the call to hand power.... wouldn't they need to reach into a bag or something for it to work?<br /> <br /> Suspend Death seems iffy to me. The Lore of Death all deals with causing death.or predicting the end, so it doesn't seem like it fits. It seems like it might fit more with Lore of the Spirit or Awakening.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you for all those points!<br /> <br /> I agree with you that the Lore selection is intentionally limited. My take is that the Fallen aren't able to access all the old connections and tools for manipulating Creation; the world and the demons themselves are too broken, too changed, for those to work like they once did. But, I also feel like a small handful of alternative Lore powers and Apocalyptic Form features could be added without hurting the setting, and might be neat elements to help characters stand out. Perhaps the character can choose to learn the &quot;canon&quot; Evocation, or learn the new &quot;alternate&quot; Evocation, but not both.<br /> <br /> I also agree with you regarding Call to Hand. I will definitely specify a requirement of pulling the object from some sort of container or (mundane) portal in the final version.<br /> <br /> As for Suspend Death, I admit that it doesn't quite fit with the other powers in the path. I kind of liked how it provided a different take on Death, but I do like your suggestion about it being part of Lore of Spirit instead. It would probably be about Spirit 3 or 4, yes? Either just before Anchor the Soul, or in place of it.<br /> <br /> Or, what about a Death or Spirit-based Evocation that was used for helping a soul to &quot;pass on&quot;, and it is the Torment version that keeps them from dying? &quot;I FORBID you to leave me!&quot;<br /> <br /> It is nice to be able to share these ideas with people who also love Demon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr />Avatar commissioned from the incomparable Melissa Uran.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/966-redford_blade","name":"Redford_Blade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar966_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"90"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-13T20:49:45-07:00","id":589840,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crowley</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/580091-demon-the-fallen-thread-for-is-better-to-rule-in-earth-than-serve-in-heaven?p=588348#post588348\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> nothing, the human host feels pleasure.<br /> <br /> in my game, depends on how much torment does the demon holds, the blood might be painful to drink. might even drive the vampire to have nightmares or visions.<br /> <br /> <br /> As for villians, if i dont bad remember, someone in the forums was working in Nephilim (I think it was you Yaoi Huntress Earth). but if im wrong i apologize.<br /> <br /> on my game i had the idea of a group of Angels that managed to &quot;Escape&quot; and &quot;Forget&quot; in a way. full angels who use and manipulate humanity into doing their bidding so they can &quot;Reach God&quot; by destroying the world for Her. very influenced by characters like Kaoru Nagisa.<br /> <br /> The other villians i had was the Dark Crussade, but rather than a villian was an organization of Wyrm Followers leaded by an Earthbound who wanted to destroy everything and leave the earth for the Childes of The Wyrm<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yeah, that was me and I've been working on some new aspects on a google doc version. Your angel idea sounds good. Is it ok if I do my own version with a Lost flock that wants to do something similar?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my DriveThruRPG books at: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?author=Carrie%20Kube\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse....=Carrie%20Kube</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1834-yaoi-huntress-earth","name":"Yaoi Huntress Earth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1834_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"535"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-13T22:01:03-07:00","id":589904,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yaoi Huntress Earth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/580091-demon-the-fallen-thread-for-is-better-to-rule-in-earth-than-serve-in-heaven?p=589840#post589840\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Yeah, that was me and I've been working on some new aspects on a google doc version. Your angel idea sounds good. Is it ok if I do my own version with a Lost flock that wants to do something similar?</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Do what <i>thou wilt</i> shall be the whole of the Law&quot;<br /> <br /> as long as my demon can make a cameo (He is walking through the WoD, trying to help and do what ever he can to keep humanity alive, he doesnt want to exploit their fate but save them rather).<br /> <br /> in my game, the angels are only 12 and they cant take a human form (like in the End of Time's book)<br /> <br /> as for the Nephilim...im pretty sure that Demons AND earthbounds would pull a truece if these Things were to appear yet again, since they are the mix of torment and humanity in a package made out of madness..so they would be a great foe to the Demons.<br /> <br /> Something that represents the Fall in a more Carnal Sense and a Taboo of existance....Now that i think about it, its pretty similar to how The Primogens feel about the new Kindread <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-14T10:58:37-07:00","id":590304,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Redford_Blade</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/580091-demon-the-fallen-thread-for-is-better-to-rule-in-earth-than-serve-in-heaven?p=589790#post589790\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Thank you for all those points!<br /> <br /> I agree with you that the Lore selection is intentionally limited. My take is that the Fallen aren't able to access all the old connections and tools for manipulating Creation; the world and the demons themselves are too broken, too changed, for those to work like they once did. But, I also feel like a small handful of alternative Lore powers and Apocalyptic Form features could be added without hurting the setting, and might be neat elements to help characters stand out. Perhaps the character can choose to learn the &quot;canon&quot; Evocation, or learn the new &quot;alternate&quot; Evocation, but not both.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Player's Guide offers an entire section on custom-building your apocalyptic form, with a great selection of powers. And yeah, a game could definitely benefit a story to give players additional powers at each point level of a Lore. Another thing I might consider, is once you've hit the end of a campaign and you're literally running the apocalypse may as well take ALL the training wheels off and give people more or less total control over their Lore areas based on how many dots they have in them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Or, what about a Death or Spirit-based Evocation that was used for helping a soul to &quot;pass on&quot;, and it is the Torment version that keeps them from dying? &quot;I FORBID you to leave me!&quot; </div> </div> </div>That makes a lot of sense!<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6883-darkexcalibur42","name":"DarkExcalibur42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6883_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-14T15:58:36-07:00","id":590553,"title":"","content":"This is one of those far out there questions, but does anyone think that a Demon can transform a Kinain into a Changeling? I suspect it would take Celestial 5 to manipulate the magical side, Humanity 5 because they are derived from human imagination, Spirit 5 to manipulate the human side of the soul, Pattern 4 or 5 to change the Kinain in the way it have could developed if it had been a Kithain rather than a Kinain, and Lore of Flesh 5 to manipulate the spiritual/metaphysical body and reshape it into something different. Maybe Lore of Radiance 5 to bring out the hidden depths of the Fae side. <br /> <br /> Any thoughts?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-14T19:46:38-07:00","id":590705,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mercurial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/580091-demon-the-fallen-thread-for-is-better-to-rule-in-earth-than-serve-in-heaven?p=590553#post590553\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is one of those far out there questions, but does anyone think that a Demon can transform a Kinain into a Changeling? I suspect it would take Celestial 5 to manipulate the magical side, Humanity 5 because they are derived from human imagination, Spirit 5 to manipulate the human side of the soul, Pattern 4 or 5 to change the Kinain in the way it have could developed if it had been a Kithain rather than a Kinain, and Lore of Flesh 5 to manipulate the spiritual/metaphysical body and reshape it into something different. Maybe Lore of Radiance 5 to bring out the hidden depths of the Fae side.<br /> <br /> Any thoughts?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think Demons have access to the very essence of reality, memories of the scattered Lores they used to literally build the universe are the source of their power. That puts them second only to Mage in terms of raw power, and possibly giving Demon a few advantages over Mages in specific scenarios. But the great machine that is the universe is decayed and rotten, turned faithless and banal through the intercession of Lucifer himself. Mages face paradox, and even demons can feel their powers diminished by the burden of human disbelief. The universe is faaaaaaaar more static and unchanging than it was in the times when the Fallen used their power with impunity. I imagine that back then, a committed demon could craft a new Lore capable of doing exactly that. But now? It would be pretty difficult to manage at all. The nearest thing I can think is that Lore of Awakening could be used in an altered way....<br /> <br /> But the Elohim didn't make the Fae: humanity did. Lucifer was intent on unlocking the potential power of humans even back during the war. In this area, I think Mages would be more able to perform this transformation than demons, though for story reasons I would definitely consider crafting a ritual to do that. Demons would be more able to convert a kinfolk into a shifting breed than a Kinain into a Changeling.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6883-darkexcalibur42","name":"DarkExcalibur42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6883_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-14T19:50:13-07:00","id":590712,"title":"","content":"tl;dr? If that's something you want to do I'd suggest writing an all new &quot;Lore of the Dreaming&quot; to use for this. During the war, the Slayers created their Lore of the Realms. This is not unlike that, in that it is a new arena of power which the Fallen had not previously influenced. But they could learn.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6883-darkexcalibur42","name":"DarkExcalibur42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6883_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-14T20:37:30-07:00","id":590779,"title":"","content":"Dreaming is a big nono in my games, The way i see it, it has to do with The Gifts and Conciense that Lucifer gives to minkdind. Something exclusive to humans","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-14T22:06:34-07:00","id":590865,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crowley</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/580091-demon-the-fallen-thread-for-is-better-to-rule-in-earth-than-serve-in-heaven?p=590779#post590779\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dreaming is a big nono in my games, The way i see it, it has to do with The Gifts and Conciense that Lucifer gives to minkdind. Something exclusive to humans</div> </div> </div> </div>So Lore of Humanity then?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-14T22:14:52-07:00","id":590888,"title":"","content":"Lore of Humanity was what they invented to control humans. Whatever Lucifer did to create the dreaming and its denizens (if in fact that really was him) is something else entirely. And many levels beyond simple manipulation.<br /> <br /> The fae seem to be very much like angels in that they are beings of faith (glamour), though they were created out of humanity's dreams rather than the Creator's will. I don't think any of the existing Lores can really be directly related to them. They're something newer and different.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6883-darkexcalibur42","name":"DarkExcalibur42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6883_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-14T22:24:34-07:00","id":590891,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mercurial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/580091-demon-the-fallen-thread-for-is-better-to-rule-in-earth-than-serve-in-heaven?p=590553#post590553\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is one of those far out there questions, but does anyone think that a Demon can transform a Kinain into a Changeling? I suspect it would take Celestial 5 to manipulate the magical side, Humanity 5 because they are derived from human imagination, Spirit 5 to manipulate the human side of the soul, Pattern 4 or 5 to change the Kinain in the way it have could developed if it had been a Kithain rather than a Kinain, and Lore of Flesh 5 to manipulate the spiritual/metaphysical body and reshape it into something different. Maybe Lore of Radiance 5 to bring out the hidden depths of the Fae side.<br /> <br /> Any thoughts?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Kinain are humans with fairy blood. Kithain are humans with fairy souls(and generally a human soul except for those dirty Sidhe). Spirit and flesh might be enough, if you can get a fairy soul from somewhere. If you're trying to make one that I'd place beyond them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-14T23:01:22-07:00","id":590951,"title":"","content":"Bond Artifact<br /> <br /> Primary Lore: <br /> Lore of Spirit 5<br /> <br /> Secondary Lore:<br /> Lore of Humanity 5<br /> Lore of Celestials 5<br /> Lore of the Firmament 3<br /> <br /> Restrictions: The Thrall and Demon must both sit in side the sigil across from each other and have a hand submerged in a gold bowl filled with an equal amount of blood from the two individuals, and both must use their free hand to grasp the relic the Demon wishes to attune himself to. If the Ankida is not the one who is attuning himself to the relic then he must place one hand over the hands of the Thrall and Demon in the bowl and another over there hands touching the relic.<br /> <br /> Base Cost: 72 <br /> <br /> Minimum Casting Time: 324 Minutes <br /> <br /> <br /> System: Roll the Ankida's Perception + Empathy. If the ritual is successful, the bond between the Demon's spiritual's essence and the Thrall's soul is so complete that the Demon can spend a temporary faith point along with a permanent point of the Thrall's Willpower in order to attune himself to a relic instead of spending a Permanent Faith to attune himself to the relic. <br /> <br /> Torment: If the ritual suffers from Torment it still works but the Thrall suffers a derangement upon the loss of the Willpower Point and the Demon attuning himself to the relic gains a Permanent Torment point as a result of wounding his Thrall's soul while so closely linked to it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-14T23:21:35-07:00","id":590959,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/580091-demon-the-fallen-thread-for-is-better-to-rule-in-earth-than-serve-in-heaven?p=590891#post590891\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Kinain are humans with fairy blood. Kithain are humans with fairy souls(and generally a human soul except for those dirty Sidhe). Spirit and flesh might be enough, if you can get a fairy soul from somewhere. If you're trying to make one that I'd place beyond them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually.... that's a really good point. If you could use a Slayer to collect a fae soul from somewhere, you could give it a new human body to reside in via the level 5 Lore of the Spirit (Restore the Dead).<br /> <br /> Yeah, you'd be putting a second soul into a body that already has one. But that's how Changelings work, isn't it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6883-darkexcalibur42","name":"DarkExcalibur42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6883_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-14T23:25:46-07:00","id":590960,"title":"","content":"Wait, if Kinain have human souls, then how do they have Perm Banality/Glamour?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-18T11:43:52-07:00","id":594883,"title":"","content":"I'd like to offer my two cents about True Faith.<br /> As we know the core limits Faith Potential to 0-5. However, in the Storyteller Companion we have rules for summoning and binding Fallen Dukes who need a host with a Faith Potential 5+.<br /> Further, later on it discusses relationships with other supernaturals to include Imbued Hunters, Mages, Werewolves, and the like. They Have Faith Potential 7-10.<br /> I personally have ruled that if a mortal host has True Faith 6+ that is the only way a mortal can surpass the Faith Potential limit of 5.<br /> Going back to the summoning and hosting of demons greater than the dregs of Infernal Society, a Fallen's Faith score is equal to the host's Potential +1.<br /> A Core Fallen starts with a Faith of 3 which informs us that they took a potential of 2 +1 for the Fallen.<br /> <br /> This is why I like the idea of starting as mortals in any WoD story, regardless of splat. Also, do not discount True Faith. It is powerful for a reason.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/15.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2104-tenkage","name":"Tenkage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2104_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-18T13:02:26-07:00","id":594922,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tenkage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/580091-demon-the-fallen-thread-for-is-better-to-rule-in-earth-than-serve-in-heaven?p=594883#post594883\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd like to offer my two cents about True Faith.<br /> As we know the core limits Faith Potential to 0-5. However, in the Storyteller Companion we have rules for summoning and binding Fallen Dukes who need a host with a Faith Potential 5+.<br /> Further, later on it discusses relationships with other supernaturals to include Imbued Hunters, Mages, Werewolves, and the like. They Have Faith Potential 7-10.<br /> I personally have ruled that if a mortal host has True Faith 6+ that is the only way a mortal can surpass the Faith Potential limit of 5.<br /> Going back to the summoning and hosting of demons greater than the dregs of Infernal Society, a Fallen's Faith score is equal to the host's Potential +1.<br /> A Core Fallen starts with a Faith of 3 which informs us that they took a potential of 2 +1 for the Fallen.<br /> <br /> This is why I like the idea of starting as mortals in any WoD story, regardless of splat. Also, do not discount True Faith. It is powerful for a reason.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Though it's worth noting that True Faith is capped at 5 as of Hunter's Hunted 2, and that demons that would be interested in getting a hold of it would probably (sunglasses) have a hell of a time accomplishing this (meetthenewbossclipmp3) due to how many powers TF5 just flat out no-sells. Demons, like vampires, are also afflicted with a supernatural fear effect when confronted with such individuals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-18T13:18:53-07:00","id":594928,"title":"","content":"I look at ToJ: Gehenna with Ferox having TF 9 as proof that True Faith is capped at 10.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/15.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2104-tenkage","name":"Tenkage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2104_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-18T15:06:46-07:00","id":595047,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tenkage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/580091-demon-the-fallen-thread-for-is-better-to-rule-in-earth-than-serve-in-heaven?p=594928#post594928\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I look at ToJ: Gehenna with Ferox having TF 9 as proof that True Faith is capped at 10.</div> </div> </div> </div>For the versions prior to the anniversary edition. The scaling was changed for HH2.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","user":"Saur Ops Specialist","date":". 07-18-2015, 06:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-18T17:32:58-07:00","id":595164,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tenkage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/580091-demon-the-fallen-thread-for-is-better-to-rule-in-earth-than-serve-in-heaven?p=594883#post594883\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd like to offer my two cents about True Faith.<br /> As we know the core limits Faith Potential to 0-5. However, in the Storyteller Companion we have rules for summoning and binding Fallen Dukes who need a host with a Faith Potential 5+.<br /> Further, later on it discusses relationships with other supernaturals to include Imbued Hunters, Mages, Werewolves, and the like. They Have Faith Potential 7-10.</div> </div> </div> </div>Demon is kinda lazy, and short-hands things here. A Hunter's Faith Potential is actually equal to their highest Virtue. This demonstrates that as supernaturally infused creatures they are more potent than ordinary people.<br /> <br /> Side note, Faith Potential is totally unrelated to True Faith, but if there were a connection I would say that it is this: humans with True Faith have a MINIMUM base of 4 Faith Potential (mmore likely the max of 5) and every point of True Faith they have after that would grant them an additional point of Faith Potential. However, no demon possessing a mortal who had previously had True Faith should really be allowed to use that Faith Potential unless the host gave itself up willingly. Storyteller ruling.<br /> <br /> That means that someone with True Faith 5 would have a Faith Potential of 10.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6883-darkexcalibur42","name":"DarkExcalibur42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6883_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-18T20:27:26-07:00","id":595321,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/580091-demon-the-fallen-thread-for-is-better-to-rule-in-earth-than-serve-in-heaven?p=595047#post595047\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> For the versions prior to the anniversary edition. The scaling was changed for HH2.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well that was dash cunning of them. I'll be honest, haven't looked at anything post-ToJ.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkExcalibur42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/580091-demon-the-fallen-thread-for-is-better-to-rule-in-earth-than-serve-in-heaven?p=595164#post595164\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Demon is kinda lazy, and short-hands things here. A Hunter's Faith Potential is actually equal to their highest Virtue. This demonstrates that as supernaturally infused creatures they are more potent than ordinary people.<br /> <br /> Side note, Faith Potential is totally unrelated to True Faith, but if there were a connection I would say that it is this: humans with True Faith have a MINIMUM base of 4 Faith Potential (mmore likely the max of 5) and every point of True Faith they have after that would grant them an additional point of Faith Potential. However, no demon possessing a mortal who had previously had True Faith should really be allowed to use that Faith Potential unless the host gave itself up willingly. Storyteller ruling.<br /> <br /> That means that someone with True Faith 5 would have a Faith Potential of 10.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was tracking that in regard to the supernaturals, I only used that to prove Faith Potential exists beyond 5.<br /> Faith Potential is unrelated yes, but I do not believe True Faith is unrelated to Faith Potential. While I don't like the cap on True Faith being limited to 5, it being the superhuman trait that bolsters mankind against the horrors of the Night without losing their humanity (in theory), I kind of like Faith Potential equaling double True Faith. And I also concur with the willing Host bit. A man of such Faith has enormous will and is hardly unclean enough to allow possession against his will. Anything that could make a man lose that will or bring him to the spiritual nadir required for suicide would also wear away at his Faith.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/15.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2104-tenkage","name":"Tenkage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2104_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-19T00:26:02-07:00","id":595458,"title":"","content":"You could have 5 dots of Truth Faith and a Willlpower of 3. True Faith doesn't reflect any greater commitment of willpower. It represents something else entirely. The reason I say the host would need to be willing is because if their will were to be broken, they would likely have lost their Faith by the time they could be inhabited. Plus it's a good plot reason to make getting high value vessels harder. Hunters are the same way: only a willing Hunter can be possessed.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6883-darkexcalibur42","name":"DarkExcalibur42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6883_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-19T01:33:29-07:00","id":595485,"title":"","content":"True Faith grants one die per point to Willpower and Virtue rolls, so in the example you mentioned, the character would have an effective willpower of 8. A character with WP 10 and TF 5 rolls 15 dice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/15.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2104-tenkage","name":"Tenkage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2104_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-20T11:41:48-07:00","id":597105,"title":"","content":"I doubt you'd have someone with both a high True Faith rating and a low Willpower score, unless it's maybe something like a saintly child.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-20T12:46:34-07:00","id":597186,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt the Bruins fan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/580091-demon-the-fallen-thread-for-is-better-to-rule-in-earth-than-serve-in-heaven?p=597105#post597105\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I doubt you'd have someone with both a high True Faith rating and a low Willpower score, unless it's maybe something like a saintly child.</div> </div> </div> </div>But that remains a possibility. The point is to demonstrate that they are unique statistics representing distinct character traits. Important to not confuse them. Which was really all I meant by it.<br /> <br /> There is also a &quot;Religious Devotion&quot; merit that grants players bonus Willpower points in specific situations. It's really cool, and a good alternate for players who think they need True Faith.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6883-darkexcalibur42","name":"DarkExcalibur42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6883_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-23T18:01:29-07:00","id":601204,"title":"","content":"New antagonists for Demon.<br /> <br /> Angels: Those still loyal to The Host. They seek out and destroy Demons on site when they get wind of their presence. They operate off Faith and equally skilled as their Demonic counterparts in the Universe's Lore.<br /> Cenobites/The Heirophants: Explorers from beyond existence. No one knows where they came from or what they do. There is a rumor that certain relics around the world can summon them for those who experience what they offer, which no one knows. Just as powerful as a Demon or Angel, but there is no counters for their abilities.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Onyx Path Kickstarters I back.<br /> W20, MtC, CB20, DtD, MtAs20, BotW20, Wraith 20th.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1442-paladindemo","name":"PaladinDemo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1442_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"622"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-24T16:12:38-07:00","id":602350,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PaladinDemo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/580091-demon-the-fallen-thread-for-is-better-to-rule-in-earth-than-serve-in-heaven?p=601204#post601204\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">New antagonists for Demon.<br /> <br /> Angels: Those still loyal to The Host. They seek out and destroy Demons on site when they get wind of their presence. They operate off Faith and equally skilled as their Demonic counterparts in the Universe's Lore.</div> </div> </div> </div>Page 90, Time of Judgement has rules for that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6883-darkexcalibur42","name":"DarkExcalibur42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6883_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-24T21:32:06-07:00","id":602550,"title":"","content":"Don't have Time of Judgement. But that'll make my work on the Cenobites easier.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Onyx Path Kickstarters I back.<br /> W20, MtC, CB20, DtD, MtAs20, BotW20, Wraith 20th.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1442-paladindemo","name":"PaladinDemo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1442_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"622"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-25T10:30:37-07:00","id":603062,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PaladinDemo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/580091-demon-the-fallen-thread-for-is-better-to-rule-in-earth-than-serve-in-heaven?p=602550#post602550\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Don't have Time of Judgement. But that'll make my work on the Cenobites easier.</div> </div> </div> </div>they could easly pass as Null Thread (Technocracy antagonists)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-25T15:02:27-07:00","id":603227,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crowley</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/580091-demon-the-fallen-thread-for-is-better-to-rule-in-earth-than-serve-in-heaven?p=603062#post603062\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> they could easly pass as Null Thread (Technocracy antagonists)</div> </div> </div> </div>I doubt their Null Void entities. Pinhead said it best.<br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=VkVsTGmQLDE\" data-code=\"VkVsTGmQLDE\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/VkVsTGmQLDE/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> They are closest to Eldrich horror you can get. Also they are also neutral, which would make great rivals for the Fallen since Cenobites don't give a shit until their summoned. Not to mention their abilities mimic the Fallen's but doesn't register in our universe.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Onyx Path Kickstarters I back.<br /> W20, MtC, CB20, DtD, MtAs20, BotW20, Wraith 20th.","edited":{"userid":1442,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1442-paladindemo","user":"PaladinDemo","date":". 07-25-2015, 06:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1442-paladindemo","name":"PaladinDemo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1442_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"622"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-27T06:12:05-07:00","id":604633,"title":"","content":"I've seen a thread around the M:tAw section called &quot;1001 Mage Story Hooks&quot; (or something along those lines) listing several short ideas for people to build upon; haven't actually reached 1001 yet but it's still a useful thing to have for those with lacking creativity, low inspiration and/or those who are better at building upon other's foundations than making said foundations themselves. Presuming it doesn't draw up too much space that would take a separate thread entirely; any such &quot;Story Hooks&quot; you can recommend for usage in a Demon game?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7060-karavolos","name":"Karavolos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7060_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"163"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-29T09:22:39-07:00","id":606674,"title":"","content":"Hapxier, one of your closest allies from the War, has recently reached out to you, asking for your help in a nearby city. When you attempt to respond to Hapxier's request, nothing happens; it is as if Hapxier no longer exists. Do you set off to follow the clues you picked up from Hapxier's last message? Has the former angel been consumed, or are they hidden away in a place where even your mental summons cannot reach?<br /> <br /> While reading a magazine, watching the news, or browsing the internet, you notice an article about a group of mortal archaeologists pulling a stone obelisk from the sea floor. The article makes wry comments about the lost city of Atlantis, but you know full well what the obelisk is. After all, you helped to put it there. What is it, and what does it mean that the mortals have found it now?<br /> <br /> While walking through your city or town, you notice that the children have been giving you odd glances out of the corners of their eyes. They think they are being discreet, but as children, they have yet to master subtlety. The adults don't seem to pay you any more attention than normal, only the children. Are the little ones being co-opted by your enemies to spy on you? Have rumors of your true nature started to spread? Or is there some utterly mundane reason for their attention?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr />Avatar commissioned from the incomparable Melissa Uran.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/966-redford_blade","name":"Redford_Blade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar966_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"90"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T00:07:46-07:00","id":609007,"title":"","content":"ill copy past this here as well, tell me what you guys think...it needs A LOT of work, but as an idea of an Internal Antagonist (and yes, i took a quoe from Wraith).<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><i><b><span style=\"color:#000000\">Host Awarness (flaw)</span></b></i></span><br /> <br /> Sometimes they come back, and sometimes they take over what it belongs to them<br /> Yes, i know that the host is technically dead and his soul is pushed away..but what if a little piece of the host is Aware somewhere deep within the chambers of the human body taken over by the Demonic Being?. One can imagine the horrors that you can witness as a &quot;Backseat passenger.&quot; This would add a new mechanic to the game.<br /> Fight for Control<br /> Every time your Demon doesnt acts according to the Human Character of the Host (For example doing things that would go against the values of the original Mortal: threating the lives of the ones close to you, use your lores to corrupt to Sin to the ones you love, destroy your own personal life etc...) the original Host (Which we will call The True Will), will be able to fight the demon from within.<br /> <br /> Each time the Fallen acts against his primal human nature within the boundries of the human host, he will get not only suspicious. but he will add a new stat called &quot;Desperation.&quot; similar to torment.<br /> <br /> Desperation works similar to the Wraith's Angst (Hell. its even a carbon sort of copy of the Shadow play).<br /> <br /> Each time the Demon attempts to do something against the host original values, he will roll his correspondant Virtue against the True Will's Desesperation (Which starts at level 3). If the demon wins, he will mantain full control of the possession no questions answered..<br /> <br /> IF the True Will wins, he will start earning temporal Desperation. These can be used to do use &quot;Glimpses.&quot;<br /> <br /> Glimpses are manifestations of the true sinister nature, a sort of &quot;Cry for Help&quot; from the inside.<br /> Example of Glimpses are<br /> Manifest an Apocaliptic Form (high level)<br /> Manifest a Lore (high Level)<br /> Speak in Tongues while Sleeping (low Level)<br /> Forcing the Damage (to make a demon actually feel pain when he is close to a holy object, even if he has low torment, high level)<br /> Book of Blood (To be able to make wounds in the demon's host body with messages to anyone outside. high level)<br /> Levitation (high level)<br /> Cold Spots (high level)<br /> Backwards Messages in Technology (low level)<br /> Mind Blasts (for the human host to be able to move objects at a max of Strg 1 and dex 1, low level)<br /> Idle Hands (for the True Will to be able to manipulate the Hand of the Demon upholding the Possession, High Level)<br /> Partial Message (for the True Will to be able to physically manifest for a number of turns equal to his permanent Desesperation. High level)<br /> Scared Animals and atract the vermin (Low level)<br /> Proyect Nightmare to a Human (High Level)<br /> Manipulation of the Shell (High Level, this involves little manipulations such as making the Demon's body not be able to blink. or manipulate the heartbeat in erratical ways, make the human body to blink with lizard like eyes, make him loose his teeths etc... This WONT CAUSE THE HOST'S BODY TO DIE. THEY ARE PURELY AESTHETHIC CHANGES)<br /> Inhumane Urges (forcing the Body Host to feed of non common meals such as bugs, dirt, nails etc.. technically speaking, nothing that would harm the body host but raise a lot of red flags)<br /> Sin of The Flesh (This one requieres to spend all the Desperation. And this one is also a shoutout to <b>Yaoi Huntress Earth. </b>The True Will has now a Deep and Intrical conection to some of the memories of the fallen one, not to those conected to the abyss; but perhaps before than that. Perhaps now the True Will has been driven mad due the Symbiotic Connection to The Monster's Mind...but now he knows what they are afraid off, What can be the living proof that Fallen ones know what is to be Afraid. The True Will can force the Fallen one to Concieve a Nephilim. <br /> If the Fallen one manages to Copulate with any mortal, the True Will may manipulate the Genetic Information of the Body in order to create a Nephilim.)<br /> <br /> How can a demon defend himself from Desperations and True Will?<br /> One: IF the demon's torment is higher than the desesperation level, he can keep control over the True Will through sheer Fear. Though, this will make the True Will to act more reckless and trying to manifest more and more to warn his loved ones<br /> Two: Acceptance, For the Fallen to be able to Comute with the True Will and manage to go through their lives and accept Death (Example: a low torment fallen would reach within his own mind and soul for the True Will and show him how he is trying to make things better, to accept the Goodness of one to protect or to say &quot;Leave it to me, ill protect your loved ones. you may rest in peace)<br /> Three: Binding Rituals, To be able to use rituals related to the Lore of Humanity in order to force the True Will fully bound and tied up (But...if it manages to set itself free through his own personal Desperation, he might be able to fuck the demon back and make people aware of the danger within itself).<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> The Desperation Mechanic:<br /> <br /> I talked a lot about these, so. How would it work?<br /> This stat goes from 1 to 10, starting at the same level of torment that the demon has.<br /> IF, the demon has this flaw (or the DM wishes to apply this mechanic). each time the fallen does a horrible inhumane act that attempts against the host's primordial nature, beliefs about values or things/people he cared about. The True Will might fight the Fallen to try and Stop it (or to give enough hints for it to be exorcised and reclaim the Flesh again...if an exorcism works, its up to the ST)<br /> <br /> Each time the demon acts against his Host' nature, he must roll for the Virtue VS the Desperation. The biggest the threat to the Original Host (or True Will), the lower the difficulty.<br /> If the ammount of successes of the Demon are Higher than the ones rolled by the True Will, the demon remains control and nothing happends.<br /> <br /> If the true will has more successes than the Demon, he may add those successes to his Desesperation Pool.<br /> The desperation might be spend to.<br /> -use a Low Level Glimpse<br /> -activate a High Level Glimpse (Costs 3 points of Desperation).<br /> -Increase the difficulty to all rolls (except for Damage rolls)<br /> Desperation can not be lowered by any other way thats not by Spending Desperation points.<br /> <br /> <br /> The whole idea of the thing is to create a new antagonist, a human trying to reach outside like a miner trapped on a mine. Knowing that someone or something is wearing his flesh and trying to find a way out by Not being Sutil. They want to break the mask of the demon so they can be released from the dak being's grasps.<br /> <br /> I just came up with the whole idea..i know theres A LOT of thingsto be fixed but what do you think?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":1754,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","user":"Crowley","date":". 07-31-2015, 03:18 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T00:38:45-07:00","id":609027,"title":"","content":"The line came far too late for me to really get into it as much as my CWoD favorites. But for the most part I did really like how they implemented the line into the CWoD metaplot. Other than the absolutely awful backstory for Lucifer and world religions I really loved the Earthbound book. My only complaint was mostly that the mechanical work on Lores was awful.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T05:14:52-07:00","id":609270,"title":"","content":"Consider the Possessed Book for W:tA. It deals with hosts, synchronicity/symbiosis and the like covering a mortal host possessed by bane, weaver, wyld, or kami spirits. You could combine it with Demon so that Fallen Angel is simply one more type of spirit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/15.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2104-tenkage","name":"Tenkage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2104_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-03T21:10:02-07:00","id":614504,"title":"","content":"what changes would you do to DtF, or any homebrew rules do you guys personally have?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-04T06:30:37-07:00","id":614949,"title":"","content":"The biggest thing that bothers me about DtF is the religious bits. Obviously there's gonna be ties, but I hate the notion that every other religion ever are just some bullshit an Earthbound made up some day while thinking of how to rule the world. So what I tend to run with is that God didn't create Earth but rather happened upon it at some point and decided to try his own hand at creation and see how it'd go. Hence he created Angels, some touches to the world mostly around the Middle-East and Adam and Lilith (and later Eve). These people however, were only the first humans created by God, not the first humans in general. Eventually rebellion and whatnot happens, God sees to the Fallen being tossed into the Abyss and puts Lucifer on Earth a l\u00e1 metaplot and then leaves with no one knowing where, why and how long presuming it's not permanent. From there I guess I run it much more in line with how I imagine most religions did come to be without adding Earthbounds to the vast majority of them. As a small note, I run things very mix-matchy between Old and New World of Darkness personally; but of note Demon is one of the only lines where I do not touch the nWoD line whatsoever due to personal distaste for it.<br /> <br /> Edit: Ps. Thanks for the ideas Redford.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7060-karavolos","name":"Karavolos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7060_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"163"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-05T00:22:20-07:00","id":616047,"title":"","content":"Crowley here from thy cellphone, so pardon my typing<br /> <br /> New Antagonist ideas!!!<br /> The Cult of The Respice Finem Mortis. <br /> A group of scholars who have get in touch with The Otherside through diferent methods, either be by temporal Death or through Ouija etc...<br /> These have discovered (through The Whispering Damned) that &quot;Hell&quot; was Made by The Fallen. And now They hunt these in order to escape OR Re-Shape this Prision and Trascend... Or Do They?<br /> The idea of these is proper fear and rejection of Death, of those trying to escape Hell (AKA Underworld)<br /> <br /> Demon's Nature<br /> I had a philodophical discusi\u00f3n about Nature and Demeanor. If They come from The demon attaching to The Human. Or if They come from The Fallen one.<br /> <br /> So, i care up with something more representativa that i Call<br /> Sinful escense: What is this?<br /> Easy, whenever your demon runs out of Willpowe or Faith , he Falls into his Sinful Nature to try and recover Willpower or Faith through other means than Reaping<br /> This means, The player must pick One of The Seven Sins which will try to guide The demon into self destructive/loathing acts until he recovers Willpower. These can be Sex with out regard of The host (Lust), Cannibalistic Rituales(Gluttonery), Acts of random Violence (Wrath) etc...<br /> <br /> Im Reworking The main mythos, thinking that theres m\u00faltiple fragmentos of god which would represent pantheon Gods (Archetypes Gods or Protogods) <br /> Or Create religions explaiming them as de interpretation of events through m\u00faltiple points of view<br /> <br /> Anything you would like me to dwelve or work On?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":1754,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","user":"Crowley","date":". 08-05-2015, 03:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-06T00:03:54-07:00","id":617216,"title":"","content":"So basically adding the nWoD Vices as an alternative to Faith and/or Willpower?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7060-karavolos","name":"Karavolos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7060_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"163"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-06T06:20:02-07:00","id":617681,"title":"","content":"Did DtF ever touch on the relationship between the Demons and Lilith? Or how do they feel about Caine and the fact he might still be running around?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my DriveThruRPG books at: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?author=Carrie%20Kube\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse....=Carrie%20Kube</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1834-yaoi-huntress-earth","name":"Yaoi Huntress Earth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1834_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"535"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-06T09:56:19-07:00","id":617832,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Karavolos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/580091-demon-the-fallen-thread-for-is-better-to-rule-in-earth-than-serve-in-heaven?p=617216#post617216\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So basically adding the nWoD Vices as an alternative to Faith and/or Willpower?</div> </div> </div> </div>Basically...yes","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-06T09:59:46-07:00","id":617833,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yaoi Huntress Earth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/580091-demon-the-fallen-thread-for-is-better-to-rule-in-earth-than-serve-in-heaven?p=617681#post617681\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Did DtF ever touch on the relationship between the Demons and Lilith? Or how do they feel about Caine and the fact he might still be running around?</div> </div> </div> </div>Sort of<br /> <br /> Days of fire mentions The Mother Of All, but is never stablished if she is eve or lilith<br /> <br /> Caine gets a mention in a novel, where a demon finds a vampire and asks &quot;Caine, is that you?&quot;<br /> <br /> Personally, i feel that most demon's hate vampires. These being representatives of everything that They hate. Or sympathy (for being cursed by god as well)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-08T18:59:03-07:00","id":657281,"title":"","content":"Can one of the Fallern learn a lore from another House?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1119-primal-flame","name":"Primal Flame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1119_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"230"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-08T21:10:46-07:00","id":657359,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primal Flame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/580091-demon-the-fallen-thread-for-is-better-to-rule-in-earth-than-serve-in-heaven?p=657281#post657281\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can one of the Fallern learn a lore from another House?</div> </div> </div> </div>Learn? if by learn you mean &quot;Absorbe his essence to gain new powers&quot;? then yes.<br /> <br /> The way i see it...ok....can you teach someone how to breath? or can you explain a person how to make your fingernails grow?...or hurmm. can you teach someone to dream (like literally dreaming).<br /> <br /> You..Cant. unless they share some of the same lores - The way I see it and interpretate it- you Cant teach what is outside of your comprehention. not because of lack of understanding, but because its something completely natural and bound to the &quot;DNA&quot; of the Fallen.<br /> You cant teach someone how you make your hair grow or how to dream. theres things that are bound to the person and that they can do or others that just cant do.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-09T07:07:48-07:00","id":657833,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primal Flame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/580091-demon-the-fallen-thread-for-is-better-to-rule-in-earth-than-serve-in-heaven?p=657281#post657281\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can one of the Fallern learn a lore from another House?</div> </div> </div> </div>The answer from the books is &quot;Yes&quot;.<br /> <br /> Though the angels are implied to have never needed to step out of their assigned roles (and thus they stuck to their House Lores), once the War started it became a necessity for the Rebels to share. As a result, it is possible to learn (or re-learn?) Lores from another House, but I believe it is only allowed after character creation.<br /> <br /> In my personal games, I will typically allow a player to start with a single dot in out-of-House Lore if it is important to their concept, but anything further requires they get training from a member of that House during the course of the story.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr />Avatar commissioned from the incomparable Melissa Uran.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/966-redford_blade","name":"Redford_Blade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar966_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"90"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-09T08:31:46-07:00","id":657917,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crowley</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/580091-demon-the-fallen-thread-for-is-better-to-rule-in-earth-than-serve-in-heaven?p=657359#post657359\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Learn? if by learn you mean &quot;Absorbe his essence to gain new powers&quot;? then yes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks, but what do you mean by absorbing the essence? Some sort of demonic diablerie? <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Redford_Blade</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/580091-demon-the-fallen-thread-for-is-better-to-rule-in-earth-than-serve-in-heaven?p=657833#post657833\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <b>The answer from the books is &quot;Yes&quot;</b>.<br /> <br /> Though the angels are implied to have never needed to step out of their assigned roles (and thus they stuck to their House Lores), once the War started it became a necessity for the Rebels to share. As a result, it is possible to learn (or re-learn?) Lores from another House, but I believe it is only allowed after character creation.<br /> <br /> In my personal games, I will typically allow a player to start with a single dot in out-of-House Lore if it is important to their concept, but anything further requires they get training from a member of that House during the course of the story.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1119-primal-flame","name":"Primal Flame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1119_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"230"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-10T09:35:32-07:00","id":659451,"title":"","content":"I have a question? Can a Demon possess a HitMark?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Reboot","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3684-david-g","name":"David G","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3684_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"176"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-11T09:25:37-07:00","id":660794,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primal Flame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/580091-demon-the-fallen-thread-for-is-better-to-rule-in-earth-than-serve-in-heaven?p=657917#post657917\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks, but what do you mean by absorbing the essence? Some sort of demonic diablerie?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, <i>exactly</i> that. Check out page 260 of the core book, under the heading &quot;Final Destruction.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>David G</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/580091-demon-the-fallen-thread-for-is-better-to-rule-in-earth-than-serve-in-heaven?p=659451#post659451\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have a question? Can a Demon possess a HitMark?</div> </div> </div> </div>Wow. I really never expected that question. Hmm.<br /> <br /> Well, most early HIT Mark models were obvious mechanical automatons, with no humanity whatsoever. The HIT Mark V models were cyborgs, utilizing a human brain inside a robot body. If anything was even slightly a candidate for possession, it would be a HIT Mark V.<br /> <br /> BUT! You could easily argue that Mark V's are not actual human beings, merely machines that happen to use an organic computer. Worse, even if a demon <i>could</i> possess them, Mark V's have none of the life experiences or emotions that serve to contain and limit Torment. A demon who possessed one would essentially be an Earthbound in a <i>mobile techno-reliquary</i>.<br /> <br /> The one possible exception would be if a mage had transferred their consciousness into the Mark V, in which case... who knows what happens?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr />Avatar commissioned from the incomparable Melissa Uran.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/966-redford_blade","name":"Redford_Blade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar966_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"90"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-11T10:03:31-07:00","id":660837,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Redford_Blade</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/580091-demon-the-fallen-thread-for-is-better-to-rule-in-earth-than-serve-in-heaven?p=660794#post660794\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes, <i>exactly</i> that. Check out page 260 of the core book, under the heading &quot;Final Destruction.&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Wow. I really never expected that question. Hmm.<br /> <br /> Well, most early HIT Mark models were obvious mechanical automatons, with no humanity whatsoever. The HIT Mark V models were cyborgs, utilizing a human brain inside a robot body. If anything was even slightly a candidate for possession, it would be a HIT Mark V.<br /> <br /> BUT! You could easily argue that Mark V's are not actual human beings, merely machines that happen to use an organic computer. Worse, even if a demon <i>could</i> possess them, Mark V's have none of the life experiences or emotions that serve to contain and limit Torment. A demon who possessed one would essentially be an Earthbound in a <i>mobile techno-reliquary</i>.<br /> <br /> The one possible exception would be if a mage had transferred their consciousness into the Mark V, in which case... who knows what happens?</div> </div> </div> </div>hurmm, i think the keyword here is Meaning.<br /> <br /> most demons who manage to possess objects. they must have a cultural significance and an emotional attachement. and lets be honest, while possessing a T800 is tempting -im having flashbacks of Terminator: Enemy Whitin. <a href=\"http://vignette3.wikia.nocookie.net/terminator/images/9/90/C890-L_biker-mods.JPG/revision/latest?cb=20081002073918\" target=\"_blank\">http://vignette3.wikia.nocookie.net/...20081002073918</a> -<br /> <br /> But, i personally believe it lacks the religious significance to be something as a &quot;Fetter&quot; for an earthbound<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-12T00:52:39-07:00","id":661641,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crowley</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/580091-demon-the-fallen-thread-for-is-better-to-rule-in-earth-than-serve-in-heaven?p=657359#post657359\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Learn? if by learn you mean &quot;Absorbe his essence to gain new powers&quot;? then yes.<br /> <br /> The way i see it...ok....can you teach someone how to breath? or can you explain a person how to make your fingernails grow?...or hurmm. can you teach someone to dream (like literally dreaming).<br /> <br /> You..Cant. unless they share some of the same lores - The way I see it and interpretate it- you Cant teach what is outside of your comprehention. not because of lack of understanding, but because its something completely natural and bound to the &quot;DNA&quot; of the Fallen.<br /> You cant teach someone how you make your hair grow or how to dream. theres things that are bound to the person and that they can do or others that just cant do.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, the way I see it, yes it makes sense for them to learn outside Lore, though with some difficulty. You have to remember that the Fallen are HYPER sensitive to the rhythms of the universe around them, meaning the Resonance. Even their powers, which are extensions of the Fallen, are sensitive to Resonance. So when you bury a Fallen in 50 Shades of the Lore of Flame, where he is acting and trying to internalize the demeanor of the Lore of Flame, have him wear clothes that resonates with the Lore, eat food that resonates with the Lore, move via a dance that resonates with the Lore while walking on flames constantly and obsidian while contemplating everything from a position to how it relates to flame, and then have a Fallen who actually knows the Lore invoke it in front of you constantly he is going to suffer from sensory overload and this will batter at the substance of what he is. But with work and willpower and time he just might be able to incorporate the spiritual truths of Flame into his being.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-17T17:26:22-07:00","id":669030,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primal Flame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/580091-demon-the-fallen-thread-for-is-better-to-rule-in-earth-than-serve-in-heaven?p=657281#post657281\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can one of the Fallern learn a lore from another House?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, in fact they have several methods to do so. they can eat another demon, be taught by another demon, and immerse yourself in trappings of that lore.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/359-dezeroth","name":"Dezeroth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar359_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"496"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-21T16:34:00-07:00","id":673531,"title":"","content":"I have a question about the Fallen and Garou. What, if any, gifts work on the Fallen. I'm asking about gifts that affect spirits, banes and such. Thanks for any help.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Reboot","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3684-david-g","name":"David G","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3684_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"176"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-21T16:41:59-07:00","id":673538,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>David G</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/580091-demon-the-fallen-thread-for-is-better-to-rule-in-earth-than-serve-in-heaven?p=673531#post673531\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have a question about the Fallen and Garou. What, if any, gifts work on the Fallen. I'm asking about gifts that affect spirits, banes and such. Thanks for any help.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's no official word on this, other than that Fallen are immune to mind control, so none of the Gifts like Obedience or True Fear will work. I'd rule that Gifts that affect Rage can affect Torment, however, and that anything that specifically targets spirits can probably do something that Fallen don't want to have happen to them, such as bleed out Faith or even kick them out of their purloined human body.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-27T12:14:43-08:00","id":838166,"title":"","content":"Heyo, im back baby!<br /> <br /> i was pondering a lot about DtF today and i came up with another little homebrow as for Factions.<br /> <br /> &quot;The Shepherds of Eden.&quot; their symbol would be an Apple with wings protecting it.<br /> <br /> The idea of this faction is basically, demons who already accepted that God is gone and that the other factions might be too Heavy (considering that most of them are literally monsters in their intentions.) So, their goal is not to achieve redemption, but rather to protect Mankind. Maybe out of sheer love and will power trying to keep the apocalypse at bay, instead of Using humans for their own goals, they want to help humans to Inherit The Earth (See what i did there?)<br /> <br /> Their weakness would be mainly to be seen as the Weaken faction, and the fact that not many share this views on humanity, embracing the idea that Every human is beautiful by definition and that every human has a chance of redemption.<br /> <br /> In a way, they are proper Luciferians by believing and trying to save mindkind.<br /> <br /> im still thinking on a faction secret.<br /> <br /> &quot;The Devilutionary Path.&quot;<br /> <br /> Basically, these basterds are not looking to save humanity, or to redeem themselves or to become Earthbounds. They trully believe that the world needs to be &quot;Rebooted.&quot;, that &quot;God Trascended into machinery.&quot; their goals its to explore the lores and the technology..As well to Evolve mankind to the next level by Creating nephilims, Trying to turn humans into Demons etc.. basically, they are the Missguided insane ones who believe that God now lies in the machine. and that Spiritual Faith has weakened so much that the only faith one can have is in the technology, to implement it and to experiment in order to create a New Eden for what ever may survive The Armageddon.<br /> These take cues from the idea of human experimentation, noticing how powerful is the science in order to control the human population.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-27T19:29:36-08:00","id":838372,"title":"","content":"In my games I've separated those who wanna protect and stand by mankind and/or the planet (Reconcilers) with those who wanna seek amendment from God and be let back into the warmth (Pentients, I'm so original with names!). There are also &quot;Unaligned Demons&quot; which I call &quot;Renegades.&quot;<br /> As far as my Reconcilers and Pentients go;<br /> The former tend to get along decently with Pentients cuz most of them seek to do good to please God and Faustians because their short-term goals both tend to benefit humanity. They do not get along at all with Raveners who are on the opposite end of the spectrum while Luciferans and Cryptics are fairly neutral.<br /> <br /> The latter, aside from Reconcilers, tend to work well with Cryptics as they feel their knowledge-seeking might solve the mystery of where God went and how to get to him. Their main opposition are the Luciferans for obvious reasons and in the long-term they would be opposed to the Faustians given the whole 'make a weapon against God' thing; though in the short-term they tend to stick away from open conflicts. Raveners are also a big enemy as to the Pentients they are the epitome of evil and even those who don't see it as a sacred duty to fight them generally want them gone because of how they ruin everything.<br /> <br /> And Renegades well, anything runs with them much like any unaligned splat.<br /> What do you think?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7060-karavolos","name":"Karavolos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7060_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"163"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-27T20:57:39-08:00","id":838431,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Karavolos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/580091-demon-the-fallen-thread-for-is-better-to-rule-in-earth-than-serve-in-heaven?p=838372#post838372\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In my games I've separated those who wanna protect and stand by mankind and/or the planet (Reconcilers) with those who wanna seek amendment from God and be let back into the warmth (Pentients, I'm so original with names!). There are also &quot;Unaligned Demons&quot; which I call &quot;