/the-classic-world-of-darkness/580091-demon-the-fallen-thread-for-is-better-to-rule-in-earth-than-serve-in-heaven?p=863459#post863459\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">cool,thanks. what are you thinking of the Lucifer tv show?</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly, im avoiding it. im sticking with the Vertigo Comic :P","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-21T15:17:38-07:00","id":870691,"title":"","content":"Since Crowley and Karavolos were posting their custom Demon factions...<br /> <br /> For my games I've created two groups. They aren't factions as much as they are Elohim who have rallied around a particular idea.<br /> <br /> The <b>Gardeners</b> are made up mostly of Devourer Reconcilers, with some other Houses mixed in. They have decided that the first step to fixing the world and setting things right, will be to return the humans to a primitive state. They intend to move slowly, so as not to cause large-scale death or disruption, but their end goal is a world without cities, without technology, where humans are few in number. Some even insist that the humans must give up their ill-gotten consciousness (like the Lightning Tree in the D:tF novels). To this end, the Gardeners are activists for voluntary population reduction (and support groups like <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Voluntary_Human_Extinction_Movement\" target=\"_blank\">VHEMT</a>), but are also looking at ways to sterilize vast swathes of the population, and are even researching advanced forms of brain surgery and lobotomies to return humans to their &quot;Pre-Fall&quot; mental state.<br /> <br /> The <b>&quot;Kill-the-Buddha Club&quot;</b> takes its name from a (misunderstood) Zen koan. A pair of Luciferans were discussing the human idea that the Creator had taken human incarnations throughout history. The idea appeared in many human faiths, and the Luciferans had noticed that there seemed to be some power that came with that faith. What if, they wondered, the Creator had actually split itself into &quot;fragments of divinity&quot;, or really did put itself into a vulnerable human form? If that were so, then the Luciferan faction could strike a real blow against the Creator, winning the War! For this reason, the group is making plans to kidnap, study, and assassinate major religious figures. Anyone who claims to be or is believed to be divine is a valid target, from monarchs who claim divine ancestry to well-known cult leaders. Since its initial formation, the group has since been quietly infiltrated by Raveners who see an opportunity to strike back at the Creator before destroying Creation itself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr />Avatar commissioned from the incomparable Melissa Uran.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/966-redford_blade","name":"Redford_Blade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar966_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"90"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-21T15:35:21-07:00","id":870707,"title":"","content":"Very nice; I'll definitely use the idea of Gardeners (a bit modified) for my universe! I also could see the KtBC being a thing if on a significantly smaller scale, good stuff.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7060-karavolos","name":"Karavolos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7060_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"163"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-21T18:16:09-07:00","id":870813,"title":"","content":"The Path of Eden.<br /> A new radical faction of Demons. Who believe that humanity has run its course and they wish to terminate almost all of human life..But two, wanting to kickstart the beginig again. To Play God as a collective by creating a new adam and eve on a post apocaliptic word...The twist, They are firm believers that God was once one of them, and that this world of darkness is nothing but a ongoing repetition of the same path..<br /> Hell, some of their most radicals even believe that God, Gaia, Wyrm. Chaos and The Weaver were original angels who survived the apocalypses. or that they been keeping the moniker and changing the subject ever since.<br /> <br /> <br /> By the way, i might have been high when i posted this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":1754,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","user":"Crowley","date":".  had extra ideas for this 04-21-2016, 09:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-22T20:27:16-07:00","id":872044,"title":"","content":"Question about Relics. . . What if a Demon enchants a pistol and gives it to the human to use it. Would the human be able to use the Relic normally without any side effects?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10423-rudy23","name":"Rudy23","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10423_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"37"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-22T20:34:08-07:00","id":872051,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rudy23</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/580091-demon-the-fallen-thread-for-is-better-to-rule-in-earth-than-serve-in-heaven?p=872044#post872044\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Question about Relics. . . What if a Demon enchants a pistol and gives it to the human to use it. Would the human be able to use the Relic normally without any side effects?</div> </div> </div> </div>theres always a side effect, read Needful things...Or Watch The Twilight Zone...or Rick and Morty","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-28T00:54:20-07:00","id":922495,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crowley</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/580091-demon-the-fallen-thread-for-is-better-to-rule-in-earth-than-serve-in-heaven?p=864272#post864272\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Honestly, im avoiding it. im sticking with the Vertigo Comic :P</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a shame because it's pretty much pure D:TF.<br /> <br /> Then again, Lucifer the comic and D:TF could not be more antithetical in purpose.<br /> <br /> Lucifer in the comic is about him being true to loathing the abridgement of free will above all things else.<br /> <br /> D:TF is about experiencing free will for the first time and choosing to exercise it.<br /> <br /> So, Lucifer the show is pretty much perfect for it.<br /> <br /> As it's about Lucifer changing, which the comic one states he never will do.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-08T11:08:09-07:00","id":928281,"title":"","content":"Got a question about how the Virtues work in comparison to Torment. I've figured out how Courage work, but Conscience and Conviction link to your personal code of ethics and your personal beliefs respectively. To what extent do you have to come up with these yourself, and how are they linked to your Torment score?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12085-beriorn","name":"Beriorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12085_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-09T05:49:34-07:00","id":928702,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Beriorn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/580091-demon-the-fallen-thread-for-is-better-to-rule-in-earth-than-serve-in-heaven?p=928281#post928281\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Got a question about how the Virtues work in comparison to Torment. I've figured out how Courage work, but Conscience and Conviction link to your personal code of ethics and your personal beliefs respectively. To what extent do you have to come up with these yourself, and how are they linked to your Torment score?</div> </div> </div> </div>running to do an examn right now.<br /> <br /> ill sum up as best as i can.<br /> basically, its to avoid you for falling into torment. to avoid your character from accepting the curse of god and his own dawnfall. to avoid you from turning into fucking regan matthews or a Deadite pretty much. the idea is that no matter how high is your torment (as long as your char is still playable), the idea of ethical redemption is always there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-12T09:38:10-07:00","id":930383,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crowley</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/580091-demon-the-fallen-thread-for-is-better-to-rule-in-earth-than-serve-in-heaven?p=928702#post928702\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">running to do an examn right now.<br /> <br /> ill sum up as best as i can.<br /> basically, its to avoid you for falling into torment. to avoid your character from accepting the curse of god and his own dawnfall. to avoid you from turning into fucking regan matthews or a Deadite pretty much. the idea is that no matter how high is your torment (as long as your char is still playable), the idea of ethical redemption is always there.</div> </div> </div> </div>Alright, but how broad or narrow should you define your ethics and beliefs? Do they have to be positive or can they be negative as well?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12085-beriorn","name":"Beriorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12085_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-01T22:29:27-07:00","id":941694,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Beriorn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/580091-demon-the-fallen-thread-for-is-better-to-rule-in-earth-than-serve-in-heaven?p=930383#post930383\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Alright, but how broad or narrow should you define your ethics and beliefs? Do they have to be positive or can they be negative as well?</div> </div> </div> </div>For that you refer to the Hierarchy of Sins, which can be found on page 159 of the core book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12205-xero_asura","name":"Xero_Asura","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12205_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-08T15:26:03-07:00","id":946509,"title":"","content":"I have a faction I haven't completely hammered out yet.<br /> <br /> A small group of fallen have found their way into the umbra proper. They have discovered realms and facets that could hail the birth of a new Eden with the right rituals worked into a realm's fabric. <br /> <br /> That is pretty much my hook for them so far","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/359-dezeroth","name":"Dezeroth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar359_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"496"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-08T15:55:35-07:00","id":946523,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dezeroth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/580091-demon-the-fallen-thread-for-is-better-to-rule-in-earth-than-serve-in-heaven?p=946509#post946509\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have a faction I haven't completely hammered out yet.<br /> <br /> A small group of fallen have found their way into the umbra proper. They have discovered realms and facets that could hail the birth of a new Eden with the right rituals worked into a realm's fabric.<br /> <br /> That is pretty much my hook for them so far</div> </div> </div> </div>Sounds like the Slayers would be all up in that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12085-beriorn","name":"Beriorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12085_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-08T16:04:50-07:00","id":946529,"title":"","content":"Nifty; do you have a name in mind for this faction?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7060-karavolos","name":"Karavolos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7060_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"163"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-09T09:21:41-07:00","id":946994,"title":"","content":"I don't have a name for the faction but I do want them poaching from the other factions or even allowing dual membership","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/359-dezeroth","name":"Dezeroth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar359_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"496"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-27T19:26:56-07:00","id":959029,"title":"","content":"Hello, just a quick question. Can a Demon use mastery to expand his natural ability to sense anything supernatural happening in his vicinity? Thanks for any help.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Reboot","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3684-david-g","name":"David G","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3684_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"176"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-27T22:32:35-07:00","id":959104,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>David G</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/580091-demon-the-fallen-thread-for-is-better-to-rule-in-earth-than-serve-in-heaven?p=959029#post959029\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hello, just a quick question. Can a Demon use mastery to expand his natural ability to sense anything supernatural happening in his vicinity? Thanks for any help.</div> </div> </div> </div>yes. the way i do it its a two way street <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-28T04:16:30-07:00","id":959170,"title":"","content":"Wait, what kind of mastery are we talking about here?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12085-beriorn","name":"Beriorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12085_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-28T05:14:17-07:00","id":959180,"title":"","content":"The background Mastery from the Earthbound book if I assume correctly. Iirc it should not be possible as of RAW as Mastery specifically affected Lores and innate powers aren't Lores. But I'd personally allow it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131211-flintys-homebrew-hub-2e\" target=\"_blank\">My Mage 2e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","name":"Flinty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"793"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-28T07:39:15-07:00","id":959238,"title":"","content":"Thank you very much for the help guys.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Reboot","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3684-david-g","name":"David G","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3684_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"176"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-26T05:22:15-07:00","id":976477,"title":"","content":"I really love Demon: The Fallen! I'd really like to play it but there is a serious lack of time with all the roleplaying stuff I'd like to try (already play in 2 pretty much weekly games and one that is 2-weekly). Also I seem to be the only one here who read any of the Demon material so I would have to be storyteller which is something I've never done before.<br /> If the opportunity ever presents itself I plan to play the adventures in Fear to Tread as I figured something like that would greatly help with my inexperience in storytelling.<br /> Any hints on what to keep in mind or what to watch out for?<br /> <br /> Something I've been thinking about recently: how do you give a Fiend with Lore of Patterns good info while not just revealing the whole plot to them? I just don't really know what I'd tell them when they're trying to predict the future or whatnot...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11694-hexer","name":"Hexer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11694_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"93"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-27T15:48:10-07:00","id":977439,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hexer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/580091-demon-the-fallen-thread-for-is-better-to-rule-in-earth-than-serve-in-heaven?p=976477#post976477\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Something I've been thinking about recently: how do you give a Fiend with Lore of Patterns good info while not just revealing the whole plot to them? I just don't really know what I'd tell them when they're trying to predict the future or whatnot...</div> </div> </div> </div>You tell them the truth... but not all of it. Trace Pattern (Patterns 2) gives you &quot;vague impressions that sharpen into detailed images as the demon devotes her unblinking attention to them&quot;, with images up to a quarter of an hour from the various forces that came up to it. Note that this only gives images, not sound or thoughts. So unless you can lipread like a boss what you actually know will be limited, so you have to make your own assumptions and deductions, something which when combined with demons will be easily twisted.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12085-beriorn","name":"Beriorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12085_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-27T23:49:15-07:00","id":977637,"title":"","content":"Fair enough, maybe I should have read it more carefully. That sounds like a good way to do it, thanks! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> Here is another question:<br /> I noticed that there is a huge difference in the possibility of a Fallen's evocations manifesting as the high-torment version between the core rulebook and the Player's Guide.<br /> <br /> In Core, the high torment version will manifest if you roll fewer successes than your torment-rating when activating an evocation which means a starting character will have to roll 3-4 successes (which is doable but not easy) to actually get the low-torment version.<br /> In the Player's Guide, the high torment version only happens if the majority of the successes you rolled show lower numbers than your torment score which basically means the high torment version will only even have a chance to occur if your torment is 7 or higher (or willingly of course). Is it permanent torment or temporary torment that is important here?<br /> <br /> Which do you go with in your games and why? Or do you have a house rule in place?<br /> I can understand why they would make it easier to manifest the low torment version of an evocation (which you probably want a lot of the times) as opposed to the core book rule but this seems like a very drastic change.<br /> I mean, if its permanent torment that is in question here, by the point you even have a chance to manifest high torment versions you'll already be manifesting high-torment abilities in your apocalyptic form and all that (you'll be way up on the torment ladder).<br /> If its temporary torment it seems quite random because why would I suddenly go back from a 100% chance to manifest high torment versions (at temp torment 10) to a 100% chance for low torment versions (at +1 permanent torment but 0 temporary)?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11694-hexer","name":"Hexer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11694_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"93"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-28T13:19:28-07:00","id":977932,"title":"","content":"With stuff like Torment and other such statted Advantages in pretty much any World of Darkness game when it's not explicitly temporary points it is pretty much always the permanent score.<br /> <br /> Personally I'd go with the Player's Guide version. If you go with the Core version you will be constantly getting the High Torment versions of your powers, which raises your Torment until you get nothing BUT the High Torment versions. One of the better kept secrets of Demon; The Fallen is that certain Abilities cover a whole slew of Lores. Survival and Medicine covers more than half of all Lores that Scourges can use. Devils need Leadership and Survival for 11 of theirs. Fiends need only Intuition to cover everything of Patterns and all but the five-dot version of Portals. Same goes for Malefactors who need Survival for Earth and Paths... then use Crafts for all the others. Devourers have Animal Ken, Medicine and Survival for all Lores in Plants, Flesh and Wild respectively. The only ones who fall outside of this are the Defilers.<br /> <br /> So you don't even really need to minmax to casually get 7-8 dice for your Lores from the get-go. Even then, consistently getting 3/4 successes is not assured, which will see you descend rather quickly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12085-beriorn","name":"Beriorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12085_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-28T22:29:36-07:00","id":978217,"title":"","content":"Absolutely! That's why I wrote I can understand that they changed it. It just seemed like an extremely drastic change to me.<br /> Well, maybe its quite ok though (the Player's Guide version) since you will rise in torment whenever you willingly manifest high-torment evocations anyways...<br /> Involuntarily they will only start to pop up at Torment 7 though and then quickly rise to 100% at Torment 10 (but this means an unplayable character anyways, so...)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11694-hexer","name":"Hexer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11694_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"93"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-29T04:05:17-07:00","id":978305,"title":"","content":"Um maybe I'm wrong but I think you only get the dot in temporary dot in torment if you deliberatly invoke the high torment evocation, not if it gets twisted because of a bad roll. At least that's how I'd play it personally. Torment should be a consequence of your actions, not bad dice rolls.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131211-flintys-homebrew-hub-2e\" target=\"_blank\">My Mage 2e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","name":"Flinty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"793"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-29T05:04:26-07:00","id":978315,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flinty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/580091-demon-the-fallen-thread-for-is-better-to-rule-in-earth-than-serve-in-heaven?p=978305#post978305\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Um maybe I'm wrong but I think you only get the dot in temporary dot in torment if you deliberatly invoke the high torment evocation, not if it gets twisted because of a bad roll. At least that's how I'd play it personally. Torment should be a consequence of your actions, not bad dice rolls.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thats correct, as I wrote above: &quot;you will rise in torment whenever you <b>willingly</b> manifest high-torment evocations&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> I have re-read some stuff in the core book though and there is a paragraph I somehow can't make sense of:<br /> &quot;If your Torment creates difficulty in using your lore (p. 169), your pain taints what you do. When you attempt to perform an evocation, compare the successes on your Faith roll against your Torment. If the successful dice all show numbers greater than your Torment, you can use the positive aspects of the power normally. If one or more of the successful dice show numbers equal to or less than your Torment score, it perverts your efforts, and you use the high-Torment aspect of the power instead.&quot;<br /> On page 169 there is the description i mentioned above (you need more successes than your Torment score to get the low-Torment version of the evocation).<br /> What &quot;Faith roll&quot; do they mean here??? Using an evocation usually requires a roll of an attribute plus a skill but not a Faith roll...<br /> <br /> Does it mean that if you get the high-torment version of an evocation involuntarily because you already have high permanent Torment, you then roll Faith against Torment (resisted? or is Torment the difficulty for the Faith roll?) to determine if you gain temp Torment or not?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11694-hexer","name":"Hexer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11694_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"93"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-29T16:43:31-07:00","id":978711,"title":"","content":"What is the exact source of that quote? I've seen the bit on page 169 it refers to, but not where that quotes comes from. While a &quot;Faith roll&quot; is a thing in Demon, it's not used a lot. It's simly a roll against your Faith, much like it would be when rolling against Willpower. See page 159 for a bit of info on Faith rolls. There it claims that certain Lores require a Faith roll, but I can't really find any.<br /> <br /> What it means though is that you have to compare the successes you roll when trying to use a Lore to your Torment. Thing is, Demon is rather poorly edited and you can run into strange things like that from time to time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12085-beriorn","name":"Beriorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12085_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-29T22:37:21-07:00","id":978869,"title":"","content":"I guess it might be a case of bad editing. It's on page 161 under &quot;Effects of Torment&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11694-hexer","name":"Hexer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11694_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"93"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-20T14:51:34-07:00","id":990647,"title":"","content":"So it's my very first time as a storyteller and none of us has ever played Demon before. <br /> We're playing the Fear to Tread chronicle and we just finished the first story with the players putting an end to an Earthbound's plans.<br /> At the end of our last session, one of my players decided that it would be fun to whisper the name of the earthbound in the middle of his fucking living room with his wife and son sleeping upstairs! We ended the session with the cliffhanger but I would like to know what my options are as a storyteller.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12577-anniehall","name":"AnnieHall","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-20T15:16:05-07:00","id":990660,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnnieHall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/580091-demon-the-fallen-thread-for-is-better-to-rule-in-earth-than-serve-in-heaven?p=990647#post990647\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> So it's my very first time as a storyteller and none of us has ever played Demon before.<br /> We're playing the Fear to Tread chronicle and we just finished the first story with the players putting an end to an Earthbound's plans.<br /> At the end of our last session, one of my players decided that it would be fun to whisper the name of the earthbound in the middle of his fucking living room with his wife and son sleeping upstairs! We ended the session with the cliffhanger but I would like to know what my options are as a storyteller.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, let's see what invoking the Celestial Name does, right? According to p.171 of the core book a Demon takes notice when their Celestial Name is spoken. By making a Faith roll (difficulty 7) a demon can determine the following based on the successes:<br /> <br /> 1: Receive a mental picture of whoever said the name.<br /> 2: That, their immediate surroundings and whoever the demon addresses.<br /> 3: That, and they can listen in on what the speaker (and just them) is saying for one turn. For every turn past that one it takes a Willpower (difficulty 8) roll.<br /> <br /> If the Earthbound in question knows the Celestial Name (or True Name, but that's pretty much a Rocks Fall scenario for that character) they can send a message to them via the rules on p.172.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12085-beriorn","name":"Beriorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12085_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-21T01:00:49-07:00","id":990843,"title":"","content":"Thank you very much for your response.<br /> <br /> It's not the mechanics that I care about. I'd like some ideas on how the Earthbound would respond to the arrogance. I mean, they just stopped his plans to increase the number of his demon servants and the guy invokes him for his own weird reasons. Given that my player loves seizing power and control(he is two weeks out of the abyss and he's already asked the tyrant of the court to remove a minister from his position-through awesome rp-) I'd loved a good idea on how I can teach him a lesson and keep him in line.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12577-anniehall","name":"AnnieHall","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-21T01:48:13-07:00","id":990861,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnnieHall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/580091-demon-the-fallen-thread-for-is-better-to-rule-in-earth-than-serve-in-heaven?p=990843#post990843\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thank you very much for your response.<br /> <br /> It's not the mechanics that I care about. I'd like some ideas on how the Earthbound would respond to the arrogance. I mean, they just stopped his plans to increase the number of his demon servants and the guy invokes him for his own weird reasons. Given that my player loves seizing power and control(he is two weeks out of the abyss and he's already asked the tyrant of the court to remove a minister from his position-through awesome rp-) I'd loved a good idea on how I can teach him a lesson and keep him in line.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, I see. Let's go with the worst case scenario: the Earthbound knows the face of whoever said its name, his face, maybe the name of some allies and the general language they speak they now have a lead on finding this particular demon. Maybe the Earthbound knows the demon in question from before the Fall? Because if so it should not be too difficult for an Earthbound with some means to track this person down and, well, make one of their agents give this demon a visit. Or if the Earthbound wants to make an example put a dead animal in the living room and use its blood to draw part of the offending demon's True Name on the wall. Don't immediately go for the family, that's dickish Storyteller behavior. Plus it does not achieve the goal that you want: you want to make him afraid, not enraged.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12085-beriorn","name":"Beriorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12085_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-21T02:50:27-07:00","id":990873,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Beriorn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/580091-demon-the-fallen-thread-for-is-better-to-rule-in-earth-than-serve-in-heaven?p=990861#post990861\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ah, I see. Let's go with the worst case scenario: the Earthbound knows the face of whoever said its name, his face, maybe the name of some allies and the general language they speak they now have a lead on finding this particular demon. Maybe the Earthbound knows the demon in question from before the Fall? Because if so it should not be too difficult for an Earthbound with some means to track this person down and, well, make one of their agents give this demon a visit. Or if the Earthbound wants to make an example put a dead animal in the living room and use its blood to draw part of the offending demon's True Name on the wall. Don't immediately go for the family, that's dickish Storyteller behavior. Plus it does not achieve the goal that you want: you want to make him afraid, not enraged.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yeah I wouldn't go for the family. He really put an effort on the background story of his host and I'd hate it to mess with the family. Also, it would lead him to a personal quest against the Earthbound leaving the other players on the outside. So, I probably go with the &quot;Godfather solution&quot; you proposed or something like that!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12577-anniehall","name":"AnnieHall","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-22T06:20:48-07:00","id":991363,"title":"","content":"If the Earthbound has any idea about the invoking characters mortal or celestial name and either he or one of his servants has knowledge of the lore of the firmament, he is going to have a bad time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131211-flintys-homebrew-hub-2e\" target=\"_blank\">My Mage 2e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","name":"Flinty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"793"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-22T17:28:14-07:00","id":991616,"title":"","content":"Has anyone heard any word on if the devs will look into a 2nd edition for dtf.<br /> <br /> This is one of my favorite games and I would love to see more of it","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/359-dezeroth","name":"Dezeroth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar359_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"496"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-23T02:29:50-07:00","id":991777,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dezeroth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/580091-demon-the-fallen-thread-for-is-better-to-rule-in-earth-than-serve-in-heaven?p=991616#post991616\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Has anyone heard any word on if the devs will look into a 2nd edition for dtf.<br /> <br /> This is one of my favorite games and I would love to see more of it</div> </div> </div> </div>It's currently unknown if there's going to be a Demon20. Given the recent reveals regarding the World of Darkness it can go either way, really.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12085-beriorn","name":"Beriorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12085_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-13T18:52:07-08:00","id":1002737,"title":"","content":"I have another question about Demons using their Lores. Can a Demon use Lore of the Spirit 5, Restore Dead bring a vampire back to life? If a vampire hasn't been embraced longer than the time limit on the lore, can the vampire be killed normally and then the lore be used to bring the dead vampire back as a human?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Reboot","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3684-david-g","name":"David G","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3684_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"176"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-13T19:34:56-08:00","id":1002748,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>David G</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/580091-demon-the-fallen-thread-for-is-better-to-rule-in-earth-than-serve-in-heaven?p=1002737#post1002737\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have another question about Demons using their Lores. Can a Demon use Lore of the Spirit 5, Restore Dead bring a vampire back to life? If a vampire hasn't been embraced longer than the time limit on the lore, can the vampire be killed normally and then the lore be used to bring the dead vampire back as a human?</div> </div> </div> </div>No. that would be WAY too overpowerful, personally the only things that might come back to life (in my games) are Average Humans....and if they Do come back, they might come back as psychopaths or deranged or in a very &quot;Zombie&quot;/Frankenstein mindstate depending on how hight the torment of the demon would be.<br /> <br /> So, no bringing back supernaturals","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-13T19:59:11-08:00","id":1002752,"title":"","content":"Thanks Crowley, it probably wouldn't work on supernaturals.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Reboot","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3684-david-g","name":"David G","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3684_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"176"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-13T21:18:09-08:00","id":1002762,"title":"","content":"Have you ever thought that WoD Earth and Hell are one of the same? No wonder why it's considered to be &quot;Worse than our world&quot; and also explains perfectly why Lucifer walks in the WoD which fits the &quot;Ruler of Hell&quot; motif since essentially, Earth from WoD IS Hell....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12524-veindark","name":"Veindark","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-13T23:00:13-08:00","id":1002776,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>David G</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/580091-demon-the-fallen-thread-for-is-better-to-rule-in-earth-than-serve-in-heaven?p=1002737#post1002737\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have another question about Demons using their Lores. Can a Demon use Lore of the Spirit 5, Restore Dead bring a vampire back to life? If a vampire hasn't been embraced longer than the time limit on the lore, can the vampire be killed normally and then the lore be used to bring the dead vampire back as a human?</div> </div> </div> </div>If the dieing vampire leaves a wraith behind, then yes you can use Spirit 5 on it. Wether the embrace made the original body unusable as a vessel sould probably be a ST call. But otherwise there is no reason they wouldn't come back. They would loose all vampire characteristics though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131211-flintys-homebrew-hub-2e\" target=\"_blank\">My Mage 2e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","name":"Flinty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"793"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-14T12:05:27-08:00","id":1002999,"title":"","content":"Thank you Flinty, while I agree with Crowley that it would make the lore very powerful, it can only be used in a very limited capacity for this situation. The base time is 48 hours or less, so there is only a very small window of opportunity. As I am the ST, I'll have to decide if I will allow it, although I am leaning to do it. Thanks again for all the input. The Demon in question has the lores for call the original soul back to the body and put it back. He is low torment so if he does this I won't have the newly raised human have any derangements from being brought back, but I might have them make a humanity roll to see if they get one from realizing what has happened.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Reboot","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3684-david-g","name":"David G","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3684_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"176"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-14T12:58:24-08:00","id":1003022,"title":"","content":"The 48 hour limit only applies to the recently dead body the soul is about to be integrated into (if a corpse is even used in the first place, a comatose body whose soul has moved on should work aswell). The Wraith (Soul) in question could have been dead for centuries, it doesn't matter. However this does not make the lore super duper powerful. If you ressurect a vampire in this way he will not come back as a vampire and he will not have any of his disciplines. He will be a normal human/risen, perhaps with a long reaching memory, but that's about it.<br /> <br /> Which takes me to the next point you need to decide upon as ST. Does Restore the dead bring back the Wraith as an actual living human or does it &quot;merely&quot; create a risen. If it creates a true mortal then he probably doesn't have any special powers, if it creates a risen it usually follows the rules for them and retains wraithly powers it had before being restored, but also still has to deal with his shadow and other drawbacks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131211-flintys-homebrew-hub-2e\" target=\"_blank\">My Mage 2e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","name":"Flinty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"793"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-15T05:35:30-08:00","id":1003338,"title":"","content":"The way I see it, if the Lore is successfully used, the vampires body is restored to life. Then the Demon places the vampire's Soul into the body. The vampire is now restored to like as a normal human, no special powers or abilities, just a long memory like you said.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Reboot","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3684-david-g","name":"David G","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3684_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"176"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-15T06:49:38-08:00","id":1003365,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>David G</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/580091-demon-the-fallen-thread-for-is-better-to-rule-in-earth-than-serve-in-heaven?p=1003338#post1003338\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The way I see it, if the Lore is successfully used, the vampires body is restored to life. Then the Demon places the vampire's Soul into the body. The vampire is now restored to like as a normal human, no special powers or abilities, just a long memory like you said.</div> </div> </div> </div>still, i think its way too op","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-15T08:35:38-08:00","id":1003417,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crowley</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/580091-demon-the-fallen-thread-for-is-better-to-rule-in-earth-than-serve-in-heaven?p=1003365#post1003365\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> still, i think its way too op</div> </div> </div> </div>In general or the specific case of reviving a vampire? I can see you having a problem with ressurrection in general, but what makes specifically reviving a vampire so op?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131211-flintys-homebrew-hub-2e\" target=\"_blank\">My Mage 2e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","name":"Flinty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"793"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-15T11:32:23-08:00","id":1003504,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>David G</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/580091-demon-the-fallen-thread-for-is-better-to-rule-in-earth-than-serve-in-heaven?p=1002737#post1002737\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have another question about Demons using their Lores. Can a Demon use Lore of the Spirit 5, Restore Dead bring a vampire back to life? If a vampire hasn't been embraced longer than the time limit on the lore, can the vampire be killed normally and then the lore be used to bring the dead vampire back as a human?</div> </div> </div> </div>I would let it work temporarily, each success above the requirements gives the vampire an additional day of life. Would be an interesting favor and way to enthrall a vampire, especially if you find a way to use it on elder vampires but the curse of Caine will always reassert itself in time","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/359-dezeroth","name":"Dezeroth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar359_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"496"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-15T19:33:54-08:00","id":1003748,"title":"","content":"The Lore in question is temporary unless the Demon spends a permanent willpower point. So with that cost, I wouldn't add any more limits.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Reboot","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3684-david-g","name":"David G","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3684_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"176"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-15T20:06:50-08:00","id":1003758,"title":"","content":"<img src=\"http://i.imgur.com/vyifrZj.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <img src=\"http://i.imgur.com/61nAjxY.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <img src=\"http://i.imgur.com/jUgMUPI.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> It's actually just under 1 in 7, not over, but whatever. I'm lazy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5307-loomer","name":"loomer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5307_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-16T20:10:10-08:00","id":1004216,"title":"","content":"What's this chart based on?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7060-karavolos","name":"Karavolos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7060_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"163"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-16T20:36:13-08:00","id":1004224,"title":"","content":"Reading every single book and seperating out duplicate entries.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5307-loomer","name":"loomer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5307_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-20T12:51:30-08:00","id":1005818,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>loomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/580091-demon-the-fallen-thread-for-is-better-to-rule-in-earth-than-serve-in-heaven?p=1004224#post1004224\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Reading every single book and seperating out duplicate entries.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Did you also create a list of all the known demons, their names, houses (if known) and location?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/412-valismedsen","name":"valismedsen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar412_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"391"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-20T16:41:57-08:00","id":1005902,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>valismedsen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/580091-demon-the-fallen-thread-for-is-better-to-rule-in-earth-than-serve-in-heaven?p=1005818#post1005818\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Did you also create a list of all the known demons, their names, houses (if known) and location?</div> </div> </div> </div>known demons? personally, i think the list would be too long considering the novels (4) , the core book, player's handbook, City of Los Angels, Earthbound, Houses of the Fallen , Fear to Thread, and the servants books. Days of fire mentions a few on the end (i belive, dont remember quite well)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-20T20:02:53-08:00","id":1005947,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>valismedsen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/580091-demon-the-fallen-thread-for-is-better-to-rule-in-earth-than-serve-in-heaven?p=1005818#post1005818\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Did you also create a list of all the known demons, their names, houses (if known) and location?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, along with every known vampire, garou, changeling, wraith, etc, containing all relevant information for each line. It's why I'm able to give a breakdown on known house and continent (by country is more revealing, but far less clean. When I finish cleaning all my data up I'll be putting out graphs to show by country as well.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crowley</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">known demons? personally, i think the list would be too long considering the novels (4) , the core book, player's handbook, City of Los Angels, Earthbound, Houses of the Fallen , Fear to Thread, and the servants books. Days of fire mentions a few on the end (i belive, dont remember quite well)</div> </div> </div> </div>The Demon list is one of the smallest compared to, say, the Vampire database. However, yes, there was and is a lot of reading to do for this project.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5307-loomer","name":"loomer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5307_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-20T21:43:11-08:00","id":1005975,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>loomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/580091-demon-the-fallen-thread-for-is-better-to-rule-in-earth-than-serve-in-heaven?p=1005947#post1005947\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes, along with every known vampire, garou, changeling, wraith, etc, containing all relevant information for each line. It's why I'm able to give a breakdown on known house and continent (by country is more revealing, but far less clean. When I finish cleaning all my data up I'll be putting out graphs to show by country as well.)<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> The Demon list is one of the smallest compared to, say, the Vampire database. However, yes, there was and is a lot of reading to do for this project.</div> </div> </div> </div>any chances to add my demon Alastor - Crowley to the list?.. i wanna be important u.u","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-20T21:51:43-08:00","id":1005981,"title":"","content":"I'm afraid not. The list only contains canon and semi-canon entities. By semi-canon, I mean vampires from the VTES card game, content from White Wolf Magazine, etc. No PCs are included.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5307-loomer","name":"loomer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5307_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-21T07:15:50-08:00","id":1006176,"title":"","content":"And any chance you could share these resources?! In any regards, I congratulate you on the good work!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/412-valismedsen","name":"valismedsen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar412_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"391"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-21T07:29:12-08:00","id":1006181,"title":"","content":"Once they're fully cleaned and pruned of duplicates etc, that's the plan. As it stands I do still need to add some of the novels and W20 content so my work is not yet done. I have another 30,000 data entries to sort through and clean as well, but the end result should be a listing of at least 30 - 40,000 unique supernatural creatures, organizations, and WoD exclusive companies like Pentex (I recorded unidentified vampires etc even with no unique characteristics, for the sake of completeness, so the figure of named creatures will be lower and of creatures with actual features lower still - so maybe 20,000 of those) and a timeline of at least 2700 unique events.<br /> <br /> The plan is to assemble the single most complete database of the oWoD ever assembled and from there establish statistical patterns of clan representation, tribes, houses, how many of each critter live where, and even ratio of representation of gender and nationality (not ethnicity except where it is very unusual, though, as by the time I thought to include that it was rather late in the game. If people pay me I can add it but the amount of manhours involved is insane.) in the published material, along with absolute minimum population ratios.<br /> <br /> For an example of that last one, I ran through the Hunter file the other day. There is an absolute minimum of 1 Imbued (including Bystanders) for every 6 million people if we take the global figure, and 1:1.3mil if we extrapolate from the disproportionate American weighting of the Imbued population. Those figures are far too low to reflect the actual game populations, but nonetheless form a bare minimum baseline that can be compared against other kinds and used as a benchmark for more representative populations. More useful is stuff like how many hunters are dead (15% or so) in the listing, how many are male or female (40% male, 18% male, with 42% unknown or ambiguous), etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5307-loomer","name":"loomer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5307_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},